te 3</td><td>32,735</td><td>35,516</td><td>36,472</td><td>34,282</td><td>32,751</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [62, 618, 719, 740], \"page_id\": 140}], \"content\": \"1 Refunds of taxes and transfer to other funds have been deducted.\\n2 Receipts of interest on investments netted by payment of interest on general fund advances.\\n3 The Highway Revenue Act of 1982 requires that, before an apportionment can be made, projected unfunded highway authorizations at the close of the fiscal year must be less than the projected net revenues for the following 24-month period, and defines \\\"unfunded\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [763, 620, 1415, 740], \"page_id\": 140}], \"content\": \"highway authorizations\\\" as the excess, if any, of (a) the total potential unpaid commitments as a result of apportionment to the States of the amounts authorized to be appropriated from the highway trust fund, over (b) the amount available in the highway trust fund at such time to defray such commitments.\\nNote.--Data is in conformance with the President's FY 1992 budget.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1377, 51, 1423, 77], \"page_id\": 141}], \"content\": \"127\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [587, 124, 897, 155], \"page_id\": 141}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUND REPORTS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [483, 314, 1096, 415], \"page_id\": 141}], \"content\": \"RECEIPTS AND OUTLAYS HIGHWAY TRUST FUND\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [607, 442, 970, 484], \"page_id\": 141}], \"content\": \"Fiscal Years 1986-90\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [76, 488, 1393, 1756], \"page_id\": 141}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [80, 51, 122, 76], \"page_id\": 142}], \"content\": \"128\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [564, 105, 939, 134], \"page_id\": 142}], \"content\": \"Inland Waterways Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [77, 178, 728, 508], \"page_id\": 142}], \"content\": \"The inland waterways trust fund was originally established on the books of the Treasury in fiscal 1981, in accordance with provisions of the Inland Waterways Revenue Act of 1978 (33 U.S.C. 1801(a)) and continued pursuant to the Water Resources Development Act of 1986 (26 U.S.C. 9506). Amounts determined by the Secretary of the Treasury to be equivalent to the amount of taxes received in the Treasury under section 4042 of the Internal Revenue Code of 1954 (relating to tax on fuel used in commercial transportation on inland waterways) shall be appropriated to the trust fund. These amounts shall be transferred at least quarterly from the general fund on the basis of estimates made by the Secretary, subject to adjustments in later transfers to the amounts of actual tax receipts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [77, 511, 729, 564], \"page_id\": 142}], \"content\": \"It shall be the duty of the Secretary of the Treasury to invest in interest-bearing obligations of the United States that portion of the\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [775, 178, 1425, 279], \"page_id\": 142}], \"content\": \"trust fund in his judgment not required to meet current withdrawals. The interest on, and the proceeds from the sale or redemption of, any obligation held in the trust fund shall be credited to and from a part of the trust fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [776, 283, 1427, 408], \"page_id\": 142}], \"content\": \"The act provides that amounts in the trust fund shall be available, by appropriations acts, for making construction and rehabilitation expenditures for navigation on the inland and intracoastal waterways of the United States described in 33 U.S.C. 1804. Expenditures must be otherwise authorized by law.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [776, 410, 1429, 537], \"page_id\": 142}], \"content\": \"Annual reports to Congress are required by 26 U.S.C. 9602(a) of the Secretary of the Treasury. These reports are required to cover the financial condition and the results of operations of the fund during the past fiscal year and its expected condition and operations during the next 5 fiscal years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [547, 615, 959, 638], \"page_id\": 142}], \"content\": \"Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 1990\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [616, 651, 903, 673], \"page_id\": 142}], \"content\": \"(Source: Financial Management Service)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [74, 671, 1425, 972], \"page_id\": 142}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 1989</td><td>$321,056,357</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Excise taxes</td><td>62,820,000</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>21,032,130</td></tr><tr><td>Accrued interest income</td><td>5,126,146</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>88,978,276</td></tr><tr><td>Expenses:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Corps of Engineers</td><td>117,258,075</td></tr><tr><td>Total expenses</td><td>117,258,075</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30, 1990</td><td>292,776,558</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [402, 1021, 1097, 1046], \"page_id\": 142}], \"content\": \"Expected Condition and Results of Operations, Fiscal Years 1991-95\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [621, 1041, 882, 1059], \"page_id\": 142}], \"content\": \"Amounts Available for Appropriation\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [74, 1064, 1425, 1362], \"page_id\": 142}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th></th><th>1991</th><th>1992</th><th>1993</th><th>1994</th><th>1995</th></tr><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1</td><td>$280.8</td><td>$249.8</td><td>$203.0</td><td>$173.6</td><td>$174.5</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Excise taxes, net of refunds</td><td>59.7</td><td>70.5</td><td>82.6</td><td>94.7</td><td>104.2</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>26.3</td><td>20.1</td><td>14.4</td><td>10.0</td><td>8.5</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>86.0</td><td>90.6</td><td>97.0</td><td>104.7</td><td>112.7</td></tr><tr><td>Appropriation</td><td>117.0</td><td>137.4</td><td>126.4</td><td>103.7</td><td>110.6</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30</td><td>249.8</td><td>203.0</td><td>173.6</td><td>174.5</td><td>176.6</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [77, 1385, 724, 1414], \"page_id\": 142}], \"content\": \"Includes accrued interest purchased and net premium or discount on investments as represented in the Budget of the United States Government, Fiscal Year 1992, and funds\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [72, 1414, 621, 1438], \"page_id\": 142}], \"content\": \"considered by Office of Management and Budget to be unrealized discounts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1375, 46, 1425, 75], \"page_id\": 143}], \"content\": \"129\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [451, 77, 1060, 115], \"page_id\": 143}], \"content\": \"Leaking Underground Storage Tank Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [75, 159, 733, 316], \"page_id\": 143}], \"content\": \"The leaking underground storage tank (LUST) trust fund was established in fiscal 1987 in accordance with provisions of the Comprehensive Environmental Response, Compensation, and Liability Act (CERCLA) of 1980 (Public Law 96-510), as amended by Superfund Amendments and Reauthorization Act (SARA) of 1986 (Public Law 99-499, dated Oct. 17, 1986).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [70, 316, 730, 446], \"page_id\": 143}], \"content\": \"The LUST trust fund is financed by taxes collected on gasoline, diesel fuels, special motor fuels, fuels in aviation, and fuels used in commercial transportation on inland waterways by the Internal Revenue Service. Other miscellaneous receipts (e.g., interest revenue) are deposited directly to the LUST trust fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [109, 446, 733, 468], \"page_id\": 143}], \"content\": \"Amounts available in the LUST trust fund, in excess of current\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [773, 161, 1428, 241], \"page_id\": 143}], \"content\": \"expenditure requirements, are invested by the Secretary of the Treasury in interest-bearing Government securities (e.g., Treasury bills). All interest earned is credited directly to the LUST trust fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [771, 241, 1425, 318], \"page_id\": 143}], \"content\": \"To carry out the LUST program, amounts are appropriated from the LUST trust fund to the Environmental Protection Agency for programmatic and administrative expenses.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [773, 318, 1425, 446], \"page_id\": 143}], \"content\": \"An annual report to Congress by the Secretary of the Treasury is required by section 9633(b)(1) of CERCLA, as amended. These reports present the financial condition of the LUST trust fund and the results of operations for the past fiscal year, and its expected condition and operations during the next 5 years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [551, 517, 952, 546], \"page_id\": 143}], \"content\": \"Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 1990\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [625, 554, 912, 583], \"page_id\": 143}], \"content\": \"(Source: Financial Management Service)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [71, 585, 1425, 1036], \"page_id\": 143}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 1989</td><td>$352,503,478</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Taxes relating to highway, inland, and airport trust funds</td><td>123,825,000</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>30,864,616</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments--accrued</td><td>3,029,246</td></tr><tr><td>Gross tax receipts</td><td>157,718,862</td></tr><tr><td>Less reimbursements to general fund:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Refund of taxes and estimated tax credits</td><td>1,753,500</td></tr><tr><td>Net receipts</td><td>155,965,362</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>155,965,362</td></tr><tr><td>Undisbursed balances:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Total undisbursed balances</td><td>-957,345</td></tr><tr><td>Expenses:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>EPA LUST expenditures</td><td>60,068,539</td></tr><tr><td>Total expenses</td><td>60,068,539</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30, 1990</td><td>449,357,646</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [401, 1087, 1095, 1115], \"page_id\": 143}], \"content\": \"Expected Condition and Results of Operations, Fiscal Years 1991-95\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [708, 1122, 794, 1146], \"page_id\": 143}], \"content\": \"(In millions)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [68, 1146, 1425, 1409], \"page_id\": 143}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th></th><th>1991</th><th>1992</th><th>1993</th><th>1994</th><th>1995</th></tr><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1</td><td>$449</td><td>$534</td><td>$662</td><td>$827</td><td>$1,017</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Taxes</td><td>109</td><td>149</td><td>152</td><td>155</td><td>157</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>45</td><td>66</td><td>97</td><td>110</td><td>118</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>154</td><td>215</td><td>249</td><td>265</td><td>275</td></tr><tr><td>Outlays</td><td>69</td><td>87</td><td>83</td><td>75</td><td>75</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30</td><td>534</td><td>662</td><td>827</td><td>1,017</td><td>1,217</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [70, 67, 114, 94], \"page_id\": 144}], \"content\": \"130\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [614, 98, 875, 127], \"page_id\": 144}], \"content\": \"Nuclear Waste Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [67, 176, 723, 328], \"page_id\": 144}], \"content\": \"The nuclear waste fund was established on the books of the Treasury in fiscal 1983, in accordance with provisions of the Nuclear Waste Policy Act of 1982 (42 U.S.C. 10222 (c)). Receipts represent fees collected from public utilities based on electricity generated by nuclear power reactors and spent nuclear fuel. Expenditures from the fund are for purposes of radioactive waste disposal activities.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [67, 332, 723, 459], \"page_id\": 144}], \"content\": \"Amounts available in the fund in excess of current needs may be invested by the Secretary of the Treasury in obligations of the United States (1) having maturities in tandem with the needs of the waste fund, and (2) bearing interest at rates determined appropriate, taking into consideration the current average market yield on outstanding\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [766, 174, 1422, 277], \"page_id\": 144}], \"content\": \"marketable obligations of the United States with remaining periods to maturity comparable to the maturities of such investments, except that the interest rate on such investments shall not exceed the average interest rate applicable to existing borrowings.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [766, 279, 1420, 404], \"page_id\": 144}], \"content\": \"An annual report to Congress by the Secretary of the Treasury, after consultation with the Secretary of Energy, is required by 42 U.S.C. 10222 (e)(1). This report must present the financial condition and the results of operations of the waste fund during the preceding fiscal year.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [544, 497, 949, 524], \"page_id\": 144}], \"content\": \"Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 1990\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [67, 526, 1425, 899], \"page_id\": 144}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th colspan=\\\"2\\\">(Source: Financial Management Service)</th><th></th></tr><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 1989</td><td></td><td>$1,196,078</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Fees collected</td><td></td><td>575,767,576</td></tr><tr><td>Penalties and interest on fee payments</td><td></td><td>1,349</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td></td><td>241,807,764</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td></td><td>817,576,689</td></tr><tr><td>Outlays:</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Department of Energy radioactive waste disposal activities</td><td></td><td>372,174,906</td></tr><tr><td>Cost of investments</td><td></td><td>444,109,076</td></tr><tr><td>Total outlays</td><td></td><td>816,283,982</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30, 1990</td><td></td><td>2,488,785</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1388, 51, 1430, 80], \"page_id\": 145}], \"content\": \"131\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [599, 102, 920, 128], \"page_id\": 145}], \"content\": \"Reforestation Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [81, 168, 740, 473], \"page_id\": 145}], \"content\": \"The reforestation trust fund was established on the books of the Treasury in fiscal year 1981 to continue through Sept. 30, 1985, in accordance with provisions of Title III--Reforestation, of the Recreational Boating Safety and Facilities Improvement Act of 1980 (16 U.S.C. 1606a (a)). The act provides that the Secretary of the Treasury shall transfer to the trust fund tariffs, limited to not more than $30 million for any fiscal year, received in the Treasury from Oct. 1, 1979, through Sept. 30, 1985, on (1) rough and primary wood products, and wood waste; (2) lumber, flooring, and moldings; and (3) wood veneers, plywood, and other wood-veneer assemblies, and building boards. Public Law 99-190 extended the receipts for the reforestation trust fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [80, 475, 736, 530], \"page_id\": 145}], \"content\": \"Amounts available in the trust fund in excess of current withdrawals are invested in interest-bearing obligations of the United\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [779, 166, 1436, 247], \"page_id\": 145}], \"content\": \"States or in obligations guaranteed as to both principal and interest by the United States. The interest on, and the proceeds from the sale or redemption of, any obligations are credited to the trust fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [781, 250, 1435, 371], \"page_id\": 145}], \"content\": \"The Secretary of Agriculture is authorized to obligate available sums in the trust fund (including any amounts not obligated in previous years) for (1) reforestation and timber stand improvement and (2) administrative costs of the Federal Government for these activities.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [779, 373, 1431, 504], \"page_id\": 145}], \"content\": \"Annual reports are required by 16 U.S.C. 1606a (c)(1) to be submitted by the Secretary of the Treasury, after consultation with the Secretary of Agriculture, on the financial condition and the results of the operations of the trust fund during the past fiscal year and on its expected condition and operations during the next fiscal year.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [556, 574, 960, 603], \"page_id\": 145}], \"content\": \"Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 1990\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [609, 616, 907, 636], \"page_id\": 145}], \"content\": \"(Source: Financial Management Service)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [75, 641, 1408, 998], \"page_id\": 145}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 1989</td><td>$3,115,283</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Tariffs</td><td>30,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>1,316,115</td></tr><tr><td>Accrued interest</td><td>50,289</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>31,366,403</td></tr><tr><td>Undisbursed balances:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Agriculture</td><td>393,247</td></tr><tr><td>Total undisbursed balances</td><td>393,247</td></tr><tr><td>Expenses:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Expenditure</td><td>2