 \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [29, 389, 1043, 651], \"page_id\": 56}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Section</th><th>1990</th><th>1991</th></tr><tr><td>Liabilities:</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>The public debt</td><td>3,233,313</td><td>3,665,303</td></tr><tr><td>Agency securities outstanding</td><td>32,758</td><td>17,751</td></tr><tr><td>Total public debt and agency securities</td><td>3,266,071</td><td>3,683,054</td></tr><tr><td>Deposit fund accounts</td><td>17,508</td><td>20,614</td></tr><tr><td>Checks and other instruments outstanding</td><td>9,066</td><td>2,814</td></tr><tr><td>Accrued interest on the public debt</td><td>43,799</td><td>42,026</td></tr><tr><td>Deferred interest (premium) on public debt subscriptions</td><td>816</td><td>823</td></tr><tr><td>Accounts payable and accruals of Government agencies, public</td><td>206,306</td><td>1 446,588</td></tr><tr><td>Total liabilities</td><td>3,543,566</td><td>4,195,919</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [31, 678, 527, 695], \"page_id\": 56}], \"content\": \"Figure includes public and Federal accounts payable and accruals of Government agencies\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [49, 710, 950, 774], \"page_id\": 56}], \"content\": \"\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [446, 781, 629, 807], \"page_id\": 56}], \"content\": \"(In billions of dollars)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [64, 810, 828, 1287], \"page_id\": 56}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [846, 803, 1080, 940], \"page_id\": 56}], \"content\": \"CHART SLOFC-A. --Commitments and Contingencies\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [850, 950, 1051, 1283], \"page_id\": 56}], \"content\": \"This report contains totals for commitments of the Government that represent the value of goods and services ordered and obligated but not yet received. It also included other commitments against appropriations, all pursuant to section 1311 of the Supplemental Appropriation Act of 1955 (31 U.S.C. 200). Contingencies represent conditional commitments that may become liabilities due to events beyond the control of the Government. The amounts are agency projections stated in terms of maximum theoretical risk exposure. The data for commitments come from agency financial statements while contingency data are from unaudited agency reports, which have not been compared with any other Treasury reports.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [87, 1305, 1020, 1324], \"page_id\": 56}], \"content\": \"Note: FMS expects to compile 1991 contingencies data by May 31, 1992. A copy of the detailed schedules can be obtained from the Financial Reports Branch (202) 208-1709.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [89, 1327, 1031, 1354], \"page_id\": 56}], \"content\": \"Amounts presented in this report were compiled from public debt budget report information and reports submitted by the agencies in accordance with Vol. I, Part 2, Chapter 4100 of the Treasury Financial Manual (Transmittal Letter No. 512). The information furnished by some reporting agencies was based on estimates.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [87, 1359, 1031, 1376], \"page_id\": 56}], \"content\": \"Sources: The Final Monthly Treasury Statement of Receipts and Outlays of the United States Government, Treasury internal documents, FMS, and the Annual Report Appendix\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1055, 43, 1076, 58], \"page_id\": 57}], \"content\": \"47\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [274, 150, 871, 209], \"page_id\": 57}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Source and Availability of the Balance in the Account of the U.S. Treasury\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [72, 238, 564, 400], \"page_id\": 57}], \"content\": \"The Treasury's operating cash is maintained in accounts with the Federal Reserve banks (FRBs) and branches, as well as in tax and loan accounts in other financial institutions. Major information sources include the Daily Balance Wire received from the FRBs and branches, and electronic transfers through the Letter of Credit Payment, Fedline Payment, and Fedwire Deposit Systems. As the FRB accounts are depleted, funds are called in (withdrawn) from thousands of tax and loan accounts at financial institutions throughout the country.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [71, 416, 565, 540], \"page_id\": 57}], \"content\": \"Under authority of Public Law 95-147, Treasury implemented a program on November 2, 1978, to invest a portion of its operating cash in obligations of depositories maintaining tax and loan accounts. Under the Treasury tax and loan investment program, depository financial institutions select the manner in which they will participate. Financial institutions wishing to retain funds deposited into their tax and loan accounts in interest-bearing obligations participate under the\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [590, 238, 1073, 380], \"page_id\": 57}], \"content\": \"Note Option. The program permits Treasury to collect funds through financial institutions and to leave the funds in Note Option depositaries and in the financial communities in which they arise until Treasury needs the funds for its operations. In this way, the Treasury is able to neutralize the effect of its fluctuating operations on Note Option financial institution reserves and on the economy. Likewise, those institutions wishing to remit the funds to the Treasury's account at FRBs do so under the Remittance Option.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [591, 399, 1077, 523], \"page_id\": 57}], \"content\": \"Deposits to tax and loan accounts occur as customers of financial institutions deposit tax payments, which the financial institutions use to purchase Government securities. In most cases, this involves a transfer of funds from a customer's account to the tax and loan account in the same financial institution. Also, Treasury can direct the FRBs to invest excess funds in tax and loan accounts directly from the Treasury account at the FRBs.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [27, 46, 54, 61], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"48\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [365, 71, 706, 90], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"ACCOUNT OF THE U.S. TREASURY\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [239, 178, 833, 230], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"TABLE UST-1.--Elements of Changes in Federal Reserve And Tax and Loan Note Account Balances\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [382, 252, 716, 271], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"(In millions of dollars. Source: Financial Management Service)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [24, 272, 1044, 690], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th rowspan=\\\"2\\\">Fiscal year or month</th><th colspan=\\\"3\\\">Federal Reserve accounts</th><th colspan=\\\"5\\\">Credits and withdrawals</th></tr><tr><th>Received directly</th><th>Received through re-mittance option tax and loan depositaries</th><th>Withdrawals 2</th><th>Proceeds from sales of securities 3</th><th>Tax and loan note accounts</th><th>Total credits</th><th>Withdrawals (transfers to Federal Reserve accounts)</th><