\"page_id\": 66}], \"content\": \"CHART FD-A.--Average Length of the Marketable Debt\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [465, 237, 615, 265], \"page_id\": 66}], \"content\": \"Privately Held\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [37, 325, 1037, 908], \"page_id\": 66}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [369, 979, 710, 996], \"page_id\": 66}], \"content\": \"Source: Department of the Treasury, Office of Market Finance\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1044, 44, 1066, 65], \"page_id\": 67}], \"content\": \"57\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [491, 66, 645, 85], \"page_id\": 67}], \"content\": \"FEDERAL DEBT\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [103, 167, 1033, 196], \"page_id\": 67}], \"content\": \"CHART FD-B.--Private Holdings of Treasury Marketable Debt, by Maturity\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [465, 230, 666, 250], \"page_id\": 67}], \"content\": \"As of December 31\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [82, 290, 1074, 891], \"page_id\": 67}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [394, 938, 733, 955], \"page_id\": 67}], \"content\": \"Source: Department of the Treasury, Office of Market Finance\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [31, 47, 52, 64], \"page_id\": 68}], \"content\": \"58\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [272, 152, 797, 181], \"page_id\": 68}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Public Debt Operations\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [30, 216, 523, 374], \"page_id\": 68}], \"content\": \"The Second Liberty Bond Act (31 U.S.C. 3101, et seq.) allows the Secretary of the Treasury to borrow money by issuing Treasury securities. The Secretary determines the terms and conditions of issue, conversion, maturity, payment, and interest rate. New issues of Treasury notes mature in 2 to 10 years. Bonds mature in more than 10 years from the issue date. Each marketable security is listed in the Monthly Statement of the Public Debt of the United States. The information in this section of the Treasury Bulletin pertains only to marketable Treasury securities, current bills, notes, and bonds.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [30, 392, 524, 512], \"page_id\": 68}], \"content\": \"Table PDO-1 provides a maturity schedule of interest-bearing marketable public debt securities other than regular weekly and 52-week bills. All unmatured Treasury notes and bonds are listed in maturity order, from earliest to latest. A separate breakout is provided for the combined holdings of the Government accounts and Federal Reserve banks, so that the \\\"all other investors\\\" category includes all private holdings.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [30, 531, 524, 597], \"page_id\": 68}], \"content\": \"Table PDO-2 presents the results of weekly auctions of 13- and 26-week bills, as well as auctions of 52-week bills, which are held every fourth week. Treasury bills mature each Thursday. New issues of 13-week bills are reopenings of 26-week bills. The 26-week bill\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [550, 216, 1034, 318], \"page_id\": 68}], \"content\": \"issued every fourth week to mature on the same Thursday as an existing 52-week bill is a reopening of the existing 52-week bill. The new issues of cash management bills are also presented. The high, low, and average yields on accepted tenders and the dollar value of total bids are presented, with the dollar value of awards made on both competitive and noncompetitive basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [551, 336, 1034, 387], \"page_id\": 68}], \"content\": \"Treasury accepts noncompetitive tenders of up to $1 million for bills and $5 million for notes and bonds in each auction of securities to encourage participation of individuals and smaller institutions.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [548, 406, 1034, 511], \"page_id\": 68}], \"content\": \"Table PDO-3 lists the results of auctions of marketable securities, other than weekly bills, in chronological order over the past 2 years. Included are: notes and bonds from table PDO-1; 52-week bills from table PDO-2; and data for cash management bills. The maturities of cash management bills coincide with those of regular issues of Treasury bills.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [550, 529, 1034, 597], \"page_id\": 68}], \"content\": \"Table PDO-4 indicates the total amount of marketable securities allotted to each class of investor. The Federal Reserve banks initially into investor classes the tenders in each auction of marketable securities other than weekly auctions of 13- and 26-week bills.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1050, 41, 1071, 58], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"59\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [432, 63, 703, 80], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"PUBLIC DEBT OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [282, 162, 849, 186], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: October-December\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [255, 267, 353, 284], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"OCTOBER\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [63, 336, 248, 349], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"Auction of 7-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [64, 378, 548, 547], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"October 2 Treasury announced it would auction $9,250 million of 7-year notes to refund $5,398 million of notes maturing October 15, 1991, and to raise about $3,850 million of new cash. The notes offered were Series H-1998, dated October 15, 1991, due October 15, 1998, with interest payable April 15 and October 15 until maturity. An interest rate of 7-1/8 percent was set after the determination of which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [63, 574, 548, 724], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"Tenders were received prior to 12:00 noon, Eastern Daylight Saving time, for noncompetitive tenders and prior to 1:00 p.m., EDST, for competitive tenders October 9, 1991, and totaled $21,626 million, of which $9,280 million was accepted at yields ranging from 7.19 percent, price 99.647, up to 7.20 percent, price 99.593. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 76 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [64, 751, 547, 833], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"Noncompetitive tenders were accepted in full at the average yield, 7.20 percent, price 99.593. These totaled $379 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $8,901 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [63, 862, 550, 966], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $9,280 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $623 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities, and $347 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks for their own account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [64, 1017, 339, 1030], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"Auction of 2-Year and 5-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [64, 1059, 548, 1165], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"October 16 Treasury announced it would auction $13,500 million of 2-year notes of Series AG-1993 and $9,000 million of 5-year notes of Series U-1996 to refund $10,636 million of securities maturing October 31, 1991, and to raise about $11,875 million of new cash.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [64, 1190, 548, 1296], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"The notes of Series AG-1993 were dated October 31, 1991, due October 31, 1993, with interest payable April 30 and October 31 until maturity. An interest rate of 6 percent was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [64, 1322, 548, 1383], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"Tenders for the notes were received prior to 12:00 noon EDST, for noncompetitive tenders and prior to 1:00 p.m. EDST, for competitive tenders October 23, and totaled\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [584, 218, 1071, 364], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"$33,423 million, of which $13,504 million was accepted at yields ranging from 6.00 percent, price 100.000, up to 6.01 percent, price 99.981. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 89 percent. Noncompetitive tenders were accepted in full at the average yield, 6.01 percent, price 99.981. These totaled $872 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $12,632 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [584, 393, 1070, 497], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $13,504 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $678 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities, and $1,486 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks for their own account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [584, 525, 1070, 628], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"The notes of Series U-1996 were dated October 31, 1991, due October 31, 1996, with interest payable April 30 and October 31 until maturity. An interest rate of 6-7/8 per cent was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [583, 656, 1070, 870], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"Tenders for the notes were received prior to 12:00 noon, EDT, for noncompetitive tenders and prior to 1:00 p.m. EDT, for competitive tenders October 24, and totaled $24,053 million, of which $9,029 million was accepted at yields ranging from 6.91 percent, price 99.854, up to 6.93 percent, price 99.771. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 13 percent. Noncompetitive tenders were accepted in full at the average yield, 6.92 percent, price 99.812. These totaled $432 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $8,597 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [584, 899, 1070, 1001], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $9,029 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $100 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities, and $200 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks for their own account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [584, 1054, 691, 1068], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"52-Week Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [584, 1097, 1071, 1202], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"October 11 tenders were invited for approximately $12,500 million of 364-day Treasury bills to be dated October 24, 1991, and to mature October 22, 1992. The issue was to refund $10,132 million of maturing 52-week bills and to raise about $2,375 million of new cash.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [584, 1231, 1070, 1380], \"page_id\": 69}], \"content\": \"Tenders were opened October 17. They totaled $36,501 million, of which $12,531 million was accepted, including $498 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public and $2,850 million of the bills issued to Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities. An additional $530 million was issued to Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international monetary\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [28, 42, 49, 61], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"60\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [393, 66, 647, 83], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"PUBLIC DEBT PERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [202, 166, 840, 191], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: October-December, Con.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [18, 230, 493, 323], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [16, 340, 504, 377], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"authorities for new cash. The average bank discount rate was 5.12 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [17, 406, 372, 421], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"Treasury Calls 7-1/2 Percent Bonds of 1988-93\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [18, 446, 506, 555], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"October 9, 1991, Treasury announced the call for redemption at par February 15, 1992, of the 7-1/2 percent Treasury bonds of 1988-93, dated August 15, 1973, due August 15, 1993. Securities not redeemed February 15, 1992, will cease to earn interest.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [18, 577, 504, 615], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"Treasury Changes Maximum Award on Noncompetitive Tenders for Notes and Bonds\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [17, 646, 506, 752], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"October 25, 1991, Treasury announced an increase in the noncompetitive bidding limit from $1 million to $5 million for notes and bonds. This change became effective with the 3-year note auction November 5, 1991. The $1 million limit for bills is unchanged.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [18, 783, 493, 884], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [19, 915, 260, 932], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"November Quarterly Financing\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [18, 957, 506, 1086], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"October 30 Treasury announced that it would auction $14,000 million of 3-year notes of Series U-1994, $12,000 million of 10-year notes of Series D-2001, and $12,000 million of 30-year bonds of November 2021 to refund $20,189 million of Treasury securities maturing November 15 and to raise about $17,800 million of new cash.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [20, 1109, 507, 1217], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"The notes of Series U-1994 were dated November 15, 1991, due November 15, 1994, with interest payable May 15 and November 15 until maturity. An interest rate of 6 percent was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [19, 1243, 507, 1371], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"Tenders for the notes were received prior to 12:00 noon, Eastern Standard time, for noncompetitive tenders and prior to 1:00 p.m., EST, for competitive tenders on November 5, and totaled $21,767 million, of which $14,000 million was accepted at yields ranging from 5.97 percent, price 100.081, up to 6.03 percent, price 99.919. Tenders at the high yield\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [539, 223, 1026, 304], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"Noncompetitive tenders were accepted in full at the average yield, 6.00 percent, price 100.00. These totaled $852 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $13,148 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [539, 331, 1027, 546], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $14,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $650 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities, and $2,135 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks for their own account. The notes of Series D-2001 were dated November 15, 1991, due November 15, 2001, with interest payable May 15 and November 15 until maturity. An interest rate of 7-1/2 percent was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [539, 573, 1027, 700], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"Tenders for the notes were received prior to 12:00 noon, EST, for noncompetitive tenders and prior to 1:00 p.m., EST, for competitive tenders November 6, and totaled $24,057 million, of which $12,004 million was accepted at yields ranging from 7.50 percent, price 100.000, up to 7.56 percent, price 99.584.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [540, 725, 1027, 830], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"Tenders at the high yield were allotted 58 percent. Non-competitive tenders were accepted in full at the average yield, 7.53 percent, price 99.792. These totaled $614 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $11,390 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [539, 861, 1027, 962], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $12,004 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $473 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities, and $300 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks for their own account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [539, 991, 1027, 1030], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"The notes of Series D-2001 may be held in STRIPS form. The minimum par amount required is $80,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [539, 1057, 1028, 1162], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"The bonds of November 2021 were dated November 15, 1991, due November 15, 2021, with interest payable May 15 and November 15 until maturity. An interest rate of 8 percent was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [540, 1190, 1029, 1317], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"Tenders for the bonds were received prior to 12:00 noon, EST, for noncompetitive tenders and prior to 1:00 p.m., EST, for competitive tenders November 7, and totaled $30,795 million, of which $12,009 million was accepted at yields ranging from 7.98 percent, price 100.227, up to 8.01 percent, price 99.887.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [540, 1344, 1026, 1381], \"page_id\": 70}], \"content\": \"Tenders at the high yield were allotted 78 percent. Non-competitive tenders were accepted in full at the average\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 22, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1045, 43, 1065, 60], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"61\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [427, 66, 698, 85], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"PUBLIC DEBT OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [244, 165, 879, 191], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: October-December, Con.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [211, 272, 391, 290], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"NOVEMBER, CON.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [59, 339, 546, 400], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"yield, 8.00 percent, price 100.000. These totaled $937 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $11,072 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [59, 426, 546, 533], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $12,009 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $150 million was accepted from FederalReserve banks for their own account. The bonds of November 2021 may be held in STRIPS form. The minimum par amount required is $25,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [60, 560, 339, 576], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"Auction of 2-Year and 5-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [60, 601, 548, 707], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"November 20 Treasury announced it would auction $13,500 million of 2-year notes of Series AH-1993 and $9,000 million of 5-year notes of Series V-1996 to refund $11,312 million of securities maturing November 30, 1991, and to raise about $11,200 million of new cash.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [61, 732, 548, 838], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"The notes of Series AH-1993 were dated December 2, 1991, due November 30, 1993, with interest payable May 31 and November 30 until maturity. An interest rate of 5-1/2 percent was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [61, 865, 550, 1083], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"Tenders for the notes were received prior to 12:00 noon, EST, for noncompetitive tenders and prior to 1:00 p.m., EST, for competitive tenders November 25, and totaled $36,350 million, of which $13,529 million was accepted at yields ranging from 5.49 percent, price 100.019, up to 5.52 percent, price 99.963. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 9 percent. Noncompetitive tenders were accepted in full at the average yield, 5.51 percent, price 99.981. These totaled $961 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $12,568 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [63, 1107, 550, 1214], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $13,529 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $979 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities, and $1,071 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks for their own account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [64, 1240, 550, 1303], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"The notes of Series V-1996 were dated December 2, 1991, due November 30, 1996, with interest payable May 31 and November 30 until maturity.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [64, 1327, 550, 1388], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"An interest rate of 6-1/2 percent was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis. Tenders for the notes were received prior to 12:00\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [579, 221, 1068, 327], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"noon, EST, for noncompetitive tenders and prior to 1:00 p.m., EST, for competitive tenders November 26, and totaled $27,096 million, of which $9,086 million was accepted at yields ranging from 6.52 percent, price 99.916, up to 6.54 percent, price 99.832.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [579, 351, 1070, 456], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"Tenders at the high yield were allotted 93 percent. Non-competitive tenders were accepted in full at the average yield, 6.54 percent, price 99.832. These totaled $827 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $8,259 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [581, 484, 1070, 589], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $9,086 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $573 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities, and $200 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks for their own account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [583, 639, 689, 656], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"52-Week Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [581, 681, 1070, 787], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"November 8 tenders were invited for approximately $12,250 million of 364-day Treasury bills to be dated November 21, 1991, and to mature November 19, 1992. The issue was to refund $12,493 million of maturing 52-week bills and to paydown about $250 million of new cash.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [581, 812, 1070, 966], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"Tenders were opened November 14. They totaled $50,773 million, of which $12,264 million was accepted, including $475 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public and $3,580 million of the bills issued to Federal Reserve banks for themselves and as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities. The average bank discount rate was 4.72 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [769, 1037, 884, 1053], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"DECEMBER\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [584, 1124, 860, 1141], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"Auction of 2-Year and 5-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [583, 1167, 1071, 1274], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"December 13 Treasury announced it would auction $13,500 million of 2-year notes of Series AJ-1993 and $9,000 million of 5-year notes of Series W-1996 to refund $17,794 million of Treasury notes maturing December 31 and to raise about $4,700 million of new cash.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [584, 1298, 1071, 1383], \"page_id\": 71}], \"content\": \"The notes of Series AJ-1993 were dated December 31, 1991, due December 31, 1993, with interest payable June 30 and December 31 until maturity. An interest rate of 5 percent was set after the determination as to which tenders were\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 22, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [33, 46, 54, 66], \"page_id\": 72}], \"content\": \"62\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [401, 73, 674, 88], \"page_id\": 72}], \"content\": \"PUBLIC DEBT OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [218, 171, 857, 196], \"page_id\": 72}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: October-December, Con.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 274, 363, 293], \"page_id\": 72}], \"content\": \"DECEMBER, CON.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [33, 343, 520, 582], \"page_id\": 72}], \"content\": \"accepted on a yield auction basis. Tenders for the notes were received prior to 12:00 noon, EST, for noncompetitive tenders and prior to 1:00 p.m., EST, for competitive tenders on December 18, and totaled $30,723 million, of which $13,505 million was accepted at yields ranging from 5.09 percent, price 99.831, up to 5.13 percent, price 99.756. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 20 percent. Noncompetitive tenders were accepted in full at the average yield, 5.12 percent, price 99.775. These totaled $891 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $12,614 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [31, 607, 520, 714], \"page_id\": 72}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $13,505 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $908 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities, and $2,091 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks for their own account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [34, 741, 521, 845], \"page_id\": 72}], \"content\": \"The notes of Series W-1996 were dated December 31, 1991, due December 31, 1996, with interest payable June 30 and December 31 until maturity. An interest rate of 6-1/8 percent was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [35, 872, 521, 911], \"page_id\": 72}], \"content\": \"Tenders for the notes were received prior to 12:00 noon, EST, for noncompetitive tenders and prior to 1:00 p.m., EST,\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [556, 227, 1043, 487], \"page_id\": 72}], \"content\": \"for competitive tenders December 19, and totaled $32,928 million, of which $9,042 million was accepted at yields ranging from 6.24 percent, price 99.513, up to 6.25 percent, price 99.470. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 6 percent. Noncompetitive tenders were accepted in full at the average yield, 6.24 percent, price 99.513. These totaled $797 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $8,245 million. In addition to the $9,042 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $373 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities, and $200 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks for their own account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [556, 534, 662, 550], \"page_id\": 72}], \"content\": \"52-Week Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [556, 577, 1043, 683], \"page_id\": 72}], \"content\": \"December 6 tenders were invited for approximately $12,250 million of 364-day Treasury bills to be dated December 19, 1991, and to mature December 17, 1992. The issue was to refund $11,799 million of maturing 52-week bills and to raise about $450 million of new cash.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [557, 708, 1043, 901], \"page_id\": 72}], \"content\": \"Tenders were opened December 12. They totaled $36,763 million, of which $12,346 million was accepted, including $426 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public and $3,100 million of the bills issued to Federal Reserve banks for themselves and as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities. An additional $1,001 million was issued to Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities for new cash. The average bank discount rate was 4.20 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [427, 66, 703, 92], \"page_id\": 73}], \"content\": \"PUBLIC DEBT OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1038, 46, 1067, 66], \"page_id\": 73}], \"content\": \"63\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [91, 160, 1032, 223], \"page_id\": 73}], \"content\": \"TABLE PDO-1.--Maturity Schedule of Interest-Bearing Marketable Public Debt Securities Other than Regular Weekly and 52-Week Treasury Bills Outstanding, Dec. 31, 1991\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [243, 228, 881, 252], \"page_id\": 73}], \"content\": \"(in millions of dollars. Source: Monthly Statement of the Public Debt of the United States, and Office of Market Finance)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [53, 249, 1072, 1364], \"page_id\": 73}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Date of final maturity</th><th>Description</th><th>Issue date</th><th>Total</th><th colspan=\\\"2\\\">Amount of maturities</th></tr><tr><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th>Held by U.S. Gov't accounts and Federal Reserve banks</th><th>All other investors</th></tr><tr><td>1992</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Jan. 15</td><td>11-5/8%-D note</td><td>01/04/85</td><td>5,759</td><td>451</td><td>5,308</td></tr><tr><td>Jan. 31</td><td>8-1/8%-V note</td><td>01/31/90</td><td>11,311</td><td>539</td><td>10,772</td></tr><tr><td>Feb. 15</td><td>14-5/8%-A note</td><td>02/16/82</td><td>2,813</td><td>215</td><td>2,598</td></tr><tr><td>Feb. 15</td><td>9-1/8%-R note</td><td>02/15/89</td><td>11,512</td><td>1,161</td><td>10,351</td></tr><tr>