id\": 160}], \"content\": \"1 Refunds of taxes and transfer to other funds have been deducted.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [25, 1236, 518, 1263], \"page_id\": 160}], \"content\": \"2 Receipts of interest on investments netted by payment of interest on general fund advances.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [27, 1263, 518, 1310], \"page_id\": 160}], \"content\": \"3 The Highway Revenue Act of 1982 requires that before an apportionment can be made projected unfunded highway authorizations at the close of the fiscal year must be less than the projected net revenues for the following 24-month period, and defines \\\"unfunded high-\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [550, 1217, 1045, 1278], \"page_id\": 160}], \"content\": \"way authorizations\\\" as the excess, if any, of (a) the total potential unpaid commitments as a result of apportionment to the States of the amounts authorized to be appropriated from the highway trust fund, over (b) the amount available in the highway trust fund at such time to defray such commitments.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [574, 1295, 946, 1309], \"page_id\": 160}], \"content\": \"Note.--Data is in conformance with the President's fiscal 1993 budget.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [461, 80, 692, 97], \"page_id\": 161}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUND REPORTS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1040, 56, 1071, 73], \"page_id\": 161}], \"content\": \"151\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [269, 175, 887, 204], \"page_id\": 161}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Inland Waterways Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [65, 228, 558, 458], \"page_id\": 161}], \"content\": \"The inland waterways trust fund was established by the Treasury in fiscal 1981, according to provisions of the Inland Waterways Revenue Act of 1978 (33 U.S.C. 1801(a)) and continued according to the Water Resources Development Act of 1986 (26 U.S.C. 9506). Amounts determined by the Secretary of the Treasury to be equivalent to the amount of taxes received in the Treasury under section 4042 of the Internal Revenue Code of 1954 (relating to tax on fuel used in commercial transportation on inland waterways) shall be appropriated to the trust fund. These amounts shall be transferred at least quarterly from the general fund based on estimates made by the Secretary, subject to adjustments in later transfers to the amounts of actual tax receipts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [63, 462, 559, 497], \"page_id\": 161}], \"content\": \"It shall be the duty of the Secretary of the Treasury to invest in interest-bearing obligations of the United States that portion of the\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [592, 227, 1084, 301], \"page_id\": 161}], \"content\": \"The interest on, and the proceeds from the sale or redemption of, any obligation held in the trust fund shall be credited to and from a part of the trust fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [594, 303, 1084, 397], \"page_id\": 161}], \"content\": \"The act provides that amounts in the trust fund shall be available, by appropriations acts, for making construction and rehabilitation expenditures for navigation on the inland and intracoastal waterways of the United States described in 33 U.S.C. 1804. Expenditures must be otherwise authorized by law.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [592, 400, 1084, 496], \"page_id\": 161}], \"content\": \"Annual reports to Congress are required by 26 U.S.C. 9602(a) of the Secretary of the Treasury. These reports are required to cover the financial condition and the results of operations of the fund during the prior fiscal year and its expected condition and operations during the next 5 fiscal years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [325, 574, 829, 634], \"page_id\": 161}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-16.--Inland Waterways Trust Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal 1991\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [469, 649, 698, 663], \"page_id\": 161}], \"content\": \"(Source: Financial Management Service)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [69, 671, 1062, 884], \"page_id\": 161}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 1990</td><td>$292,776,558</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Excise taxes</td><td>60,483,000</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>24,669,494</td></tr><tr><td>Accrued interest income</td><td>-3,453,832</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>81,698,662</td></tr><tr><td>Expenses:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Corps of Engineers</td><td>148,568,530</td></tr><tr><td>Total expenses</td><td>148,568,530</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30, 1991</td><td>225,906,629</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [222, 957, 940, 990], \"page_id\": 161}], \"content\": \"Expected Condition and Results of Operations, Fiscal Years 1992-96\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [529, 993, 641, 1005], \"page_id\": 161}], \"content\": \"(In millions of dollars)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [67, 1007, 1070, 1226], \"page_id\": 161}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th></th><th>1992</th><th>1993</th><th>1994</th><th>1995</th><th>1996</th></tr><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1<sup>1</sup></td><td>216.9</td><td>178.2</td><td>157.3</td><td>147.4</td><td>146.5</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Excise taxes, net of refunds</td><td>70.5</td><td>82.6</td><td>94.7</td><td>104.2</td><td>109.4</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>15.8</td><td>11.8</td><td>10.7</td><td>10.2</td><td>10.2</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>86.3</td><td>94.4</td><td>105.4</td><td>114.4</td><td>118.6</td></tr><tr><td>Appropriation</td><td>125.0</td><td>115.3</td><td>115.3</td><td>115.3</td><td>115.3</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30</td><td>178.2</td><td>157.3</td><td>147.4</td><td>146.5</td><td>149.8</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [69, 1250, 559, 1279], \"page_id\": 161}], \"content\": \"1 Includes unrealized discounts on investments as represented in the Budget of the United States Government, Fiscal Year 1993.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [31, 54, 78, 81], \"page_id\": 162}], \"content\": \"152\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [418, 74, 664, 110], \"page_id\": 162}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUND REPORTS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [162, 178, 927, 216], \"page_id\": 162}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Leaking Underground Storage Tank Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [29, 242, 527, 367], \"page_id\": 162}], \"content\": \"The Leaking Underground Storage Tank (LUST) Trust Fund was established in fiscal 1971 according to provisions of the Comprehensive Environmental Response, Compensation, and Liability Act (CERCLA) of 1980 (Public Law 96-510), as amended by Superfund Amendments and Reauthorization Act (SARA) of 1986 (Public Law 99-499, dated October 17, 1986).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [23, 364, 530, 497], \"page_id\": 162}], \"content\": \"The LUST trust fund is financed by taxes collected on gasoline, diesel fuels, special motor fuels, fuels in aviation, and fuels used in commercial transportation on inland waterways by the Internal Revenue Service. Other miscellaneous receipts (e.g., interest revenue) are deposited directly to the LUST trust fund. Amounts available in the LUST trust fund, exceeding current expenditure requirements,\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [553, 247, 1049, 309], \"page_id\": 162}], \"content\": \"are invested by the Secretary of the Treasury in interest-bearing Government securities (e.g., Treasury bills). All interest earned is credited directly to the LUST trust fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [551, 308, 1053, 369], \"page_id\": 162}], \"content\": \"To carry out the LUST program, amounts are appropriated from the LUST trust fund to the Environmental Protection Agency for programmatic and administrative expenses.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [550, 367, 1051, 472], \"page_id\": 162}], \"content\": \"An annual report to Congress by the Secretary of the Treasury is required by section 9633(b)(1) of CERCLA, as amended. These reports present the financial condition of the LUST trust fund and the results of operations for the past fiscal year, and its expected condition and operations during the next fiscal 5 years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [228, 563, 855, 621], \"page_id\": 162}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-17.--Leaking Underground Storage Tank Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal 1991\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [418, 627, 659, 658], \"page_id\": 162}], \"content\": \"[Source: Financial Management Service]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [19, 659, 1045, 1070], \"page_id\": 162}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 1990</td><td>$448,400,301</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Taxes relating to highway, inland, and airport trust funds</td><td>123,251,000</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>32,800,680</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments\\u2014accrued</td><td>2,528,069</td></tr><tr><td>Gross tax receipts</td><td>158,579,749</td></tr><tr><td>Less reimbursements to general fund:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Refund of taxes and estimated tax credits</td><td>550,000</td></tr><tr><td>Net receipts</td><td>158,129,749</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>158,129,749</td></tr><tr><td>Outlays:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Inspector general</td><td>75,000</td></tr><tr><td>Total outlays</td><td>75,000</td></tr><tr><td>Undisbursed balances:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Total undisbursed balances</td><td>27,250,465</td></tr><tr><td>Expenses:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>EPA LUST expenditures</td><td>42,692,189</td></tr><tr><td>Total expenses</td><td>42,692,189</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30, 1991</td><td>$36,512,396</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [182, 1111, 900, 1140], \"page_id\": 162}], \"content\": \"Expected Condition and Results of Operations, Fiscal Years 1992-96\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [460, 1141, 620, 1168], \"page_id\": 162}], \"content\": \"(In millions of dollars)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [28, 1165, 1045, 1390], \"page_id\": 162}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th></th><th>1992</th><th>1993</th><th>1994</th><th>1995</th><th>1996</th></tr><tr><td>Balance Oct.</td><td>$536.5</td><td>$629.2</td><td>$725.2</td><td>$834.6</td><td>$947.6</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Taxes relating to highway, inland and airport trust funds</td><td>145.0</td><td>147.0</td><td>150.0</td><td>152.0</td><td>155.0</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>34.5</td><td>35.7</td><td>35.7</td><td>36.2</td><td>36.9</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>179.5</td><td>182.7</td><td>185.7</td><td>188.2</td><td>191.9</td></tr><tr><td>Outlays</td><td>86.8</td><td>86.7</td><td>76.3</td><td>75.2</td><td>75.0</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30</td><td>629.2</td><td>725.2</td><td>834.6</td><td>947.6</td><td>1,064.5</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [438, 75, 670, 92], \"page_id\": 163}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUND REPORTS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1027, 49, 1057, 66], \"page_id\": 163}], \"content\": \"153\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [274, 172, 834, 198], \"page_id\": 163}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Nuclear Waste Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [47, 225, 536, 337], \"page_id\": 163}], \"content\": \"The nuclear waste fund was established on the books of the Treasury in fiscal 1983, according to provisions of the Nuclear Waste Policy Act of 1982 (42 U.S.C. 10222 (c)). Receipts represent fees collected from public utilities based on electricity generated by nuclear power reactors and spent nuclear fuel. Expenditures from the fund are for purposes of radioactive waste disposal activities.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [47, 339, 536, 416], \"page_id\": 163}], \"content\": \"Amounts available in the fund exceeding current needs may be invested by the Secretary of the Treasury in obligations of the United States (1) having maturities in tandem with the needs of the waste fund, and (2) bearing interest at rates determined appropriate, taking\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [573, 223, 1060, 318], \"page_id\": 163}], \"content\": \"into consideration the current average market yield on outstanding marketable obligations of the United States with remaining periods to maturity comparable to the maturities of such investments, except that the interest rate on such investments shall not exceed the average interest rate applicable to existing borrowings.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [573, 322, 1060, 416], \"page_id\": 163}], \"content\": \"An annual report to Congress by the Secretary of the Treasury after consultation with the Secretary of Energy, is required by 42 U.S.C. 10222 (e)(1). This report must present the financial condition and the results of operations of the waste fund during the preceding fiscal year.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [361, 538, 746, 591], \"page_id\": 163}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-18.--Nuclear Waste Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal 1991\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [448, 610, 662, 620], \"page_id\": 163}], \"content\": \"(Source: Financial Management Service)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [44, 635, 1029, 843], \"page_id\": 163}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 1990</td><td>$ 2,488,785</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Fees collected</td><td>604,699,716</td></tr><tr><td>Penalties and interest on fee payments</td><td>5,536</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>305,312,046</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>910,015,298</td></tr><tr><td>Outlays:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Department of Energy radioactive waste disposal activities</td><td>315,047,989</td></tr><tr><td>Cost of investments</td><td>595,338,324</td></tr><tr><td>Total outlays</td><td>910,386,313</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30, 1991</td><td>2,117,770</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [28, 46, 61, 68], \"page_id\": 164}], \"content\": \"154\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [416, 71, 653, 91], \"page_id\": 164}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUND REPORTS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [257, 164, 810, 200], \"page_id\": 164}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Reforestation Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [28, 216, 518, 477], \"page_id\": 164}], \"content\": \"The reforestation trust fund was established on the books of the Treasury in fiscal 1981 to continue through September 30, 1985, according to provisions of Title III\\u2014Reforestation, of the Recreational Boating Safety and Facilities Improvement Act of 1980 (16 U.S.C. 1606a (a)). The act provides that the Secretary of the Treasury shall transfer to the trust fund tariffs, limited to not more than $30 million for any fiscal year, received in the Treasury from October 1, 1979, through September 30, 1985, on (1) rough and primary wood products, and wood waste; (2) lumber, flooring, and moldings; and (3) wood veneers, plywood, and other wood-veneer assemblies, and building boards. Public Law 99-190 extended the receipts for the trust fund. Amounts available in the reforestation fund exceeding current\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [550, 215, 1044, 477], \"page_id\": 164}], \"content\": \"withdrawals are invested in interest-bearing obligations of the United States or in obligations guaranteed as to both principal and interest by the United States. The interest on, and the proceeds from the sale or redemption of, any obligations are credited to the trust fund.\\nThe Secretary of Agriculture is authorized to obligate available sums in the trust fund (including any amounts not obligated in previous years) for (1) reforestation and timber stand improvement and (2) administrative costs of the Government for these activities.\\nAnnual reports are required by 16 U.S.C. 1606a (c)(1) to be submitted by the Secretary of the Treasury, after consultation with the Secretary of Agriculture, on the financial condition and the results of the operations of the trust fund during the past fiscal year and on its expected condition and operations during the next fiscal year.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [312, 610, 752, 670], \"page_id\": 164}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-19.--Reforestation Trust Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal 1991\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [422, 680, 644, 697], \"page_id\": 164}], \"content\": \"(Source: Financial Management Service)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [24, 710, 1005, 915], \"page_id\": 164}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 1990</td><td>$396,268</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Tariffs Excise taxes (Tariffs)</td><td>30,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>30,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>Expenses:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Expenditure</td><td>22,650,855</td></tr><tr><td>Total expenses</td><td>22,650,855</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30, 1991</td><td>7,745,413</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [229, 1004, 835, 1030], \"page_id\": 164}], \"content\": \"Expected Condition and Results of Operations, Fiscal 1992\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [459, 1040, 595, 1057], \"page_id\": 164}], \"content\": \"(In thousands of dollars)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [24, 1070, 1005, 1229], \"page_id\": 164}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 1991</td><td>7,745</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Excise taxes (Tariffs)</td><td>30,000</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>350</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>30,350</td></tr><tr><td>Outlays</td><td>30,350</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30</td><td>7,745</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1034, 27, 1082, 72], \"page_id\": 165}], \"content\": \"155\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [429, 56, 675, 99], \"page_id\": 165}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUND REPORTS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [238, 206, 963, 255], \"page_id\": 165}], \"content\": \"CHARTS TF-D AND E.--Major Trust Funds\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [329, 262, 591, 334], \"page_id\": 165}], \"content\": \"Fiscal 1990 and 1991 (In billions of dollars)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [50, 336, 1018, 1320], \"page_id\": 165}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1030, 39, 1065, 65], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"157\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [469, 61, 656, 111], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Glossary\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [197, 164, 921, 198], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Expanded, With References to Applicable Sections and Tables\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [71, 254, 552, 380], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Accrued discount (SBN-1, -2, -3)\\u2014Interest that accumulates on savings bonds from the date of purchase until the date of redemption or final maturity, whichever comes first. Series A, B, C, D, E, EE, F, and J are discount or accrual type bonds\\u2014meaning principal and interest are paid when bonds are redeemed. Series G, H, HH, and K are current-income bonds, and the semiannual interest paid to their holders is not included in accrued discount.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [71, 393, 551, 484], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Amounts outstanding and in circulation (USCC)--Includes all issues by the Bureau of the Mint purposely intended as a medium of exchange. Coins sold by the Bureau of the Mint at premium prices are excluded; however, uncirculated coin sets sold at face value plus handling charge are included.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [72, 499, 552, 572], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Average discount rate (PDO-2, -3)-In Treasury bill auctions, purchasers tender competitive bids on a discount rate basis. The average discount rate is the weighted, or adjusted, average of all bids accepted in the auction.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [72, 584, 551, 697], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Budget authority (\\\"Federal Fiscal Operations\\\")\\u2014Congress passes laws giving budget authority to Government entities, which gives the agencies the power to spend Federal funds. Congress can stipulate various criteria for the spending of these funds. For example, Congress can stipulate that a given agency must spend within a specific year, number of years, or any time in the future.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [71, 708, 551, 853], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"The basic forms of budget authority are appropriations, authority to borrow, and contract authority. The period of time during which Congress makes funds available may be specified as 1-year, multiple-year, or no-year. The available amount may be classified as either definite or indefinite; a specific amount or an unspecified amount can be made available. Authority may also be classified as current or permanent. Permanent authority requires no current action by Congress.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [71, 867, 551, 904], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Budget deficit--The total, cumulative amount by which budget outlays (spending) exceed budget receipts (income).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [71, 920, 552, 957], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Capital (\\\"Federal Obligations\\\")--Assets, such as land, equipment, and financial reserves.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [72, 972, 551, 1063], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Cash management bills (PDO-2)--Marketable Treasury bills of irregular maturity lengths, sold periodically to fund short-term cash needs of Treasury. Their sale, having higher minimum and multiple purchase requirements than those of other issues, is generally restricted to competitive bidders.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [71, 1080, 551, 1153], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Competitive tenders (\\\"Treasury Financing Operations\\\")\\u2014A bid to purchase a stated amount of one issue of Treasury securities at a specified yield or discount. The bid is accepted if it is within the range accepted in the auction. (See noncompetitive tenders.)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [70, 1167, 499, 1189], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Coupon Issue--The issue of bonds or notes (public debt).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [71, 1202, 551, 1255], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Currency no longer Issued (USCC)\\u2014Old and new series gold and silver certificates, Federal Reserve notes, national bank notes, and 1890 Series Treasury notes.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [72, 1272, 552, 1328], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Current Income bonds (\\\"U.S. Savings Bonds and Notes\\\")-Bonds paying semiannual interest to holders. Interest is not included in accrued discount.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [71, 1342, 552, 1415], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Debt outstanding subject to limitation (FD-6)\\u2014The debt incurred by the Treasury subject to the statutory limit set by Congress. Until World War I, a specific amount of debt was authorized to each separate security issue. Beginning with the Second Liberty Loan\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [581, 254, 1052, 327], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Act of 1917, the nature of the limitation was modified, until in 1941, it developed into an overall limit on the outstanding Federal debt. In 1991, the debt limit was $4,145,000 million; the limit may change from year to year.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [583, 341, 1052, 433], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"The debt subject to limitation includes most of Treasury's public debt except of securities issued to the Federal Financing Bank, upon which there is a limitation of $15 billion, and certain categories of older debt (totaling approximately $595 million as of February 1991).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [583, 446, 1052, 487], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Discount--The interest deducted in advance when purchasing notes or bonds. (see Accrued discount)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [583, 499, 1052, 591], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Discount rate (PDO-2)--The difference between par value and the actual purchase price paid, annualized over a 360-day year. Because this rate is less than the actual yield (coupon-equivalent rate), the yield should be used in any comparison with coupon issue securities.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [581, 605, 1052, 644], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Dollar coins (USCC)--Dollar coins include standard silver and nonsilver coins.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [583, 657, 1052, 748], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Domestic series (FD-2)\\u2014Nonmarketable, interest and non-interest-bearing securities issued periodically by Treasury to the Resolution Funding Corporation (RFC) for investment of funds authorized under section 21B of the Federal Home Loan Bank Act (12 U.S.C. 1441b).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [583, 761, 1052, 835], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Federal Intrafund transactions (\\\"Federal Fiscal Operations\\\") -Intrabudgetary transactions in which payments and receipts both occur within the same Federal fund group (either Federal funds or trust funds).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 22, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [583, 850, 1052, 961], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Federal Reserve notes (USCC)--Issues by the U.S. Government to the public through the Federal Reserve banks and their member banks. They represent money owed by the Government to the public. Currently, the item \\\"Federal Reserve notes--amounts outstanding\\\" consists of new series issues. The Federal Reserve note is the only class of currency currently issued.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 23, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [583, 976, 1052, 1030], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Foreign (\\\"Foreign Currency Positions,\\\" IFS-2, -3)--(international) Locations other than those included under the definition of the United States. (See United States.)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 24, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [583, 1044, 1054, 1208], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Foreigner (\\\"Capital Movements,\\\" IFS-2)\\u2014All institutions and individuals living outside the United States, including U.S. citizens living abroad, and branches, subsidiaries, and other affiliates abroad of U.S. banks and business concerns; central governments, central banks, and other official institutions of countries other than the United States, and international and regional organizations, wherever located. Also, refers to persons in the United States to the extent that they are known by reporting institutions to be acting for foreigners.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 25, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [583, 1221, 1052, 1417], \"page_id\": 167}], \"content\": \"Foreign public borrower ('Capital Movements')--Central governments and departments of central governments of foreign countries and of their possessions; foreign central banks, stabilization funds, and exchange authorities, corporations and other agencies of central governments, including development banks and institutions, and other agencies that are majority-owned by the central government or its departments. Also included are state, provincial, and local governments of foreign countries, and their departments and agencies; and any international or regional organization or subordinate or affiliate, created by treaty or convention between sovereign states.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 26, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [28, 52, 60, 68], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"158\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [380, 73, 688, 117], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"Glossary, Con.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [43, 189, 521, 331], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"Foreign-targeted issue (PDO-1,-3)\\u2014Foreign-targeted issues were notes sold between October 1984 and February 1986 to foreign institutions, foreign branches of U.S. institutions, foreign central banks or monetary authorities, or to international organizations in which the United States held membership. Sold as companion issues, they could be converted to domestic (normal) Treasury notes with the same maturity and interest rates. Interest was paid annually rather than semiannually.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [45, 347, 522, 384], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"Fractional coins (USCC)--Coins minted in denominations of 50, 25, and 10 cents, and minor coins (5 cents and 1 cent).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [43, 401, 522, 593], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"Government account series (FD-2)\\u2014Certain trust fund statutes require the Secretary of the Treasury to apply monies held by these funds toward the issuance of nonmarketable special securities. These securities are sold directly by Treasury to a specific Government agency, trust fund, or account. Their rate is based on an average of market yields on outstanding Treasury obligations, and they may be redeemed at the option of the holder. Roughly 80 percent of these are issued to five holders: the Federal old-age and survivors insurance trust fund; the civil service retirement and disability fund; the Federal hospital insurance trust fund; the military retirement fund; and the unemployment trust fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [45, 610, 524, 680], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"International Monetary Fund (\\\"Exchange Stabilization Fund\\\" IFS-1)--(IMF) Established by the United Nations, the IMF promotes international trade, stability of exchange, and monetary cooperation. Members are allowed to draw from the fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [45, 697, 524, 752], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"Interfund transactions (\\\"Federal Fiscal Operations\\\")--Transactions in which payments are made from one fund group (either Federal funds or trust funds) to a receipt account in another group.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [45, 768, 524, 857], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"Intrabudgetary transactions (\\\"Federal Fiscal Operations\\\")\\u2014Intrabudgetary transactions occur when payment and receipt both occur within the budget, or when payment is made from off-budget Federal entities whose budget authority and outlays are excluded from the budget totals.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [47, 874, 524, 962], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"Majority-owned foreign partnerships (\\\"Foreign Currency Positions\\\")\\u2014Partnerships organized under the laws of a foreign country in which one or more nonbanking concerns or nonprofit institutions in the United States, directly or indirectly, owns more than 50 percent profit interest.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [47, 981, 524, 1086], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"Majority-owned foreign subsidiaries (\\\"Foreign Currency Positions\\\")--Foreign corporations in which one or more nonbanking business concerns or nonprofit institutions located in the United States, directly or indirectly, owns stock with more than 50 percent of the total combined voting power, or more than 50 percent of the total value of all classes of stock.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [48, 1102, 524, 1261], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"Matured non-interest-bearing debt (SBN-1, -2, -3)-The value of outstanding savings bonds and notes that have reached final maturity and no longer earn interest. This includes all Series A-D, F, G, J, and K bonds. Series E bonds (issued between May 1941 and November 1965) have a final maturity of 30 years, as do Series EE (issued since January 1980). Series H (issued from June 1952 through December 1979), and savings notes issued between May 1967 and October 1970. Series HH bonds (issued since January 1980) mature after 20 years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [48, 1280, 526, 1366], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"Noncompetitive tenders (\\\"Treasury Financing Operations\\\")\\u2014Offers by an investor to purchase Treasury securities at the price equivalent to the weighted average discount rate or yield of accepted competitive tenders in a Treasury auction. Noncompetitive tenders are always accepted in full.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [51, 1383, 524, 1419], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"Obligation (\\\"Federal Obligations\\\")--An unpaid commitment to acquire goods or services.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [554, 188, 1023, 293], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"Off-budget Federal entities (\\\"Federal Fiscal Operations\\\")- Federally owned and controlled entities whose transactions are excluded from the budget totals under provisions of law. Their receipts, outlays, and surplus or deficit are not included in budget receipts, outlays, or deficits. Their budget authority is not included in the totals of the budget.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [557, 311, 1023, 364], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"Outlays--(expenditures, net disbursements) Payments on obligations in the form of cash, checks, the issuance of bonds or notes, or the maturing of interest coupons.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [556, 382, 1020, 397], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"Par value--The face value of bonds or notes, including interest.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [556, 414, 1023, 558], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"Quarterly financing (\\\"Treasury Financing Operations\\\")\\u2014 Treasury has historically offered packages of several \\\"coupon\\\" security issues on the 15th of February, May, August, and November, or on the next working day. These issues currently consist of a 3-year note, a 10-year note, and a 30-year bond. Treasury sometimes offers additional amounts of outstanding long-term notes or bonds, rather than selling new security issues (See reopening.)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [557, 573, 1025, 626], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"Receipts (\\\"Federal Fiscal Operations\\\")\\u2014Funds collected from selling land, capital, or services, as well as collections from the public (budget receipts), such as taxes, fines, duties, and fees.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [557, 644, 1026, 714], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"Reopening (PDO-3, -4)-The offer for sale of additional amounts of outstanding issues, rather than an entirely new issue. A reopened issue will always have the same maturity date, CUSIP number, and interest rate as the original issue.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [557, 730, 1026, 766], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"Short-term (\\\"Foreign Currency Positions\\\")--Securities maturing in 1 year or less.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [558, 785, 1026, 874], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"Special drawing rights (\\\"Exchange Stabilization Fund,\\\" IFS-1) - (SDRs) International assets created by IMF that serve to increase international liquidity and provide additional international reserves. They may be purchased and sold among eligible holders through IMF. (See IMF)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [558, 891, 1027, 996], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"SDR allocations are the counterpart to SDRs issued by IMF based on members' quotas in IMF. Although shown in exchange stabilization fund (ESF) statements as liabilities, they must be redeemed by ESF only in the event of liquidation of, or United States withdrawal from, the SDR department of IMF or cancellation of SDRs.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [559, 1015, 1027, 1082], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"SDR certificates are issued to the Federal Reserve System against SDRs when SDRs are legalized as money. Proceeds of monetization are deposited into an ESF account at the Federal Reserve Bank of New York.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 22, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [559, 1101, 1027, 1136], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"\\\"Spot\\\" (\\\"Foreign Currency Positions\\\")--Due for receipt or delivery within 2 workdays.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 23, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [559, 1155, 1027, 1312], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"State and local government series (FD-2)\\u2014(SLUGS) Special nonmarketable certificates, notes, and bonds offered to State and local governments as a means to invest proceeds from their own tax-exempt financing. Interest rates and maturities comply with IRS arbitrage provisions. SLUGS are offered in both time deposit and demand deposit forms. Time deposit certificates have maturities of up to 1 year. Notes mature in 1 to 10 years and bonds mature in more than 10 years. Demand deposit securities are 1-day certificates rolled over with a rate adjustment daily.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 24, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [560, 1331, 1027, 1419], \"page_id\": 168}], \"content\": \"Statutory debt limit (FD-6)\\u2014By Act of Congress there is a limit, either temporary or permanent, on the amount of public debt that may be outstanding. When this limit is reached, the Treasury may not sell new debt issues until Congress increases or extends the limit. For a detailed listing of the changes in the limit since 1941;\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 25, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1045, 41, 1082, 65], \"page_id\": 169}], \"content\": \"159\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [90, 179, 570, 221], \"page_id\": 169}], \"content\": \"refer to the Budget of the United States Government. (See debt outstanding subject to limitation.)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [90, 230, 569, 344], \"page_id\": 169}], \"content\": \"STRIPS (PDO-1, -3)-Separate Trading of Registered Interest and Principal Securities. Long-term notes and bonds may be divided into principal and interest-paying components, which may be transferred and sold in amounts as small as $1,000. STRIPS are sold at auction at a minimum par amount, varying for each issue. The amount is an arithmetic function of the issue's interest rate.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [90, 353, 569, 395], \"page_id\": 169}], \"content\": \"Treasury bills--The shortest term Federal security (maturity dates normally varying from 3 to 12 months), they are sold at a discount.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [90, 405, 563, 429], \"page_id\": 169}], \"content\": \"Trust fund transaction (\\\"Federal Fiscal Operations\\\")--An intra-\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [600, 179, 1067, 223], \"page_id\": 169}], \"content\": \"budgetary transaction in which both payments and receipts occur within the same trust fund group.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [600, 232, 1070, 293], \"page_id\": 169}], \"content\": \"United States--Includes the 50 States, District of Columbia, Commonwealth of Puerto Rico, American Samoa, Midway Island, Virgin Islands, and Wake Island.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [600, 301, 1071, 363], \"page_id\": 169}], \"content\": \"U.S. notes (USCC)\\u2014Legal tender notes of five different issues: 1862 ($5-$1,000 notes); 1862 ($1-$2 notes); 1863 ($5-$1,000 notes); 1863 ($1-$10,000 notes); and 1901 ($10 notes).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [600, 371, 1068, 414], \"page_id\": 169}], \"content\": \"Worldwide (\\\"Foreign Currency Position\\\")\\u2014Sum of \\\"United States and \\\"foreign\\\" trade.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [424, 58, 735, 112], \"page_id\": 169}], \"content\": \"Glossary, Con.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1043, 53, 1084, 87], \"page_id\": 171}], \"content\": \"161\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [396, 94, 762, 141], \"page_id\": 171}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bulletin User Survey\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [52, 150, 1101, 232], \"page_id\": 171}], \"content\": \"In order to assist the Financial Reports Branch in our efforts to revise and improve our publication, please take a few moments to answer the following questions. Your responses will enable us to enhance the quality of the bulletin in order to meet your needs better.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [77, 284, 390, 312], \"page_id\": 171}], \"content\": \"Name/organization, telephone number:\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [75, 318, 197, 341], \"page_id\": 171}], \"content\": \"Job function:\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [67, 353, 884, 375], \"page_id\": 171}], \"content\": \"How often do you use the Treasury Bulletin? [ ] Daily [ ] Weekly [ ] Monthly [ ] Quarterly [ ] Yearly\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [66, 388, 238, 410], \"page_id\": 171}], \"content\": \"For what purpose?\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [70, 409, 882, 431], \"page_id\": 171}], \"content\": \"1 Investment purposes 11 Report Preparation 11 School/Work 11 Economic Predictions 11 Other\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [70, 438, 737, 467], \"page_id\": 171}], \"content\": \"How valuable is the Treasury Bulletin to your work?\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [72, 473, 298, 496], \"page_id\": 171}], \"content\": \"What sections do you use?\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [72, 496, 722, 642], \"page_id\": 171}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>[ ] Articles</td><td>[ ] U.S. Savings Bonds & Notes</td></tr><tr><td>[ ] Profile of the Economy</td><td>[ ] Ownership of Federal Securities</td></tr><tr><td>[ ] Federal Fiscal Operations</td><td>[ ] Market Yields</td></tr><tr><td>[ ] Federal Obligations</td><td>[ ] Federal Agencies' Financial Reports</td></tr><tr><td>[ ] Account of the U.S. Treasury</td><td>[ ] International Financial Statistics</td></tr><tr><td>[ ] Federal Debt</td><td>[ ] Capital Movements</td></tr><tr><td>[ ] Treasury Financing Operations</td><td>[ ] Foreign Currency Positions</td></tr><tr><td>[ ] Public Debt Operations</td><td>[ ] Exchange Stabilization Fund</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [754, 492, 1078, 620], \"page_id\": 171}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>1] Consolidated Financial Statements of the United States Government</td></tr><tr><td>1] Statement of Liabilities/Other Financial Commitments</td></tr><tr><td>1] Trust Fund Reports</td></tr><tr><td>1] U.S. Currency & Coin</td></tr><tr><td>1] Glossary</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [69, 640, 733, 678], \"page_id\": 171}], \"content\": \"Is the information presented in a manner you can use/understand? [ ] Yes [ ] No\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [67, 685, 449, 714], \"page_id\": 171}], \"content\": \"Do you find the graphs helpful? [ ] Yes [ ] No\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [72, 719, 695, 821], \"page_id\": 171}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td colspan=\\\"2\\\">Would you like to see the Treasury Bulletin provide...? (check those that apply)</td></tr><tr><td>[ ] more policy papers</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>[ ] Interviews with Treasury officials</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>[ ] more data; explain</td><td>___________________________________</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [40, 714, 60, 835], \"page_id\": 171}], \"content\": \"Cut on dotted line.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [86, 828, 358, 923], \"page_id\": 171}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>[ ] better presentation; explain</td></tr><tr><td>[ ] easier to understand tables</td></tr><tr><td>[ ] computer data access</td></tr><tr><td>[ ] more graphs</td></tr><tr><td>[ ] expanded sections; which ones?</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [87, 932, 156, 957], \"page_id\": 171}], \"content\": \"[] other\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [72, 1032, 751, 1063], \"page_id\": 171}], \"content\": \"What other suggestions or comments do you have for improving the Treasury Bulletin?\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [347, 1354, 829, 1436], \"page_id\": 171}], \"content\": \"We appreciate your participation in this survey. Please detach, fold, and staple so that the address on the reverse side is visible.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [12, 61, 47, 78], \"page_id\": 172}], \"content\": \"162\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [12, 544, 427, 615], \"page_id\": 172}], \"content\": \"DEPARTMENT OF THE TREASURY\\nFINANCIAL MANAGEMENT SERVICE\\nWASHINGTON, D.C. 20227\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [72, 663, 346, 700], \"page_id\": 172}], \"content\": \"OFFICIAL BUSINESS PENALTY FOR PRIVATE USE, $300\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [353, 758, 799, 847], \"page_id\": 172}], \"content\": \"DEPARTMENT OF THE TREASURY\\nFINANCIAL MANAGEMENT SERVICE\\n941 NORTH CAPITOL STREET, NE., ROOM 703\\nWASHINGTON, DC 20227\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [871, 544, 986, 666], \"page_id\": 172}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [796, 697, 1049, 758], \"page_id\": 172}], \"content\": \"POSTAGE AND FEES PAID DEPARTMENT OF THE TREASURY 553\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 49, 915, 78], \"page_id\": 175}], \"content\": \"Information about the Superintendent of Documents Subscription Service\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [21, 104, 195, 128], \"page_id\": 175}], \"content\": \"Current Subscribers\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [18, 128, 1038, 203], \"page_id\": 175}], \"content\": \"To know when to expect your renewal notice and keep a good thing coming ... to keep subscription prices down, the Government Printing Office mails each subscriber only one renewal notice. You can learn when you will get your renewal notice by checking the number that follows ISSDUE on the top line of your label as shown in this example:\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [21, 203, 899, 387], \"page_id\": 175}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td colspan=\\\"2\\\">When this digit is 0, a renewal notice will be sent.</td></tr><tr><td>TRBU SMITH212J</td><td>ISSDUE000 R 1</td></tr><tr><td>JOHN SMITH</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>212 MAIN ST</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>FORESTVILLE MD 20747</td><td></td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [21, 392, 1043, 450], \"page_id\": 175}], \"content\": \"When that number reads ISSDUE000, you have received your last issue unless you renew. You should receive your renewal notice around the same time that you receive the issue with ISSDUE000 on the top line.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [18, 465, 1044, 548], \"page_id\": 175}], \"content\": \"To be sure that your service continues without interruption, please return your renewal notice promptly. If your subscription service is discontinued, simply send your mailing label from any issue to the Superintendent of Documents, Washington, DC 20402-9372 with the proper remittance, and your service will be reinstated.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [17, 560, 1041, 620], \"page_id\": 175}], \"content\": \"To change your address . . . please SEND YOUR MAILING LABEL, along with your new address, to the Superintendent of Documents, Attn: Chief, Mail List Branch, Mail Stop: SSOM, Washington, DC 20402-9373.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [15, 630, 1044, 691], \"page_id\": 175}], \"content\": \"To inquire about your subscription service... please SEND YOUR MAILING LABEL, along with your correspondence, to the Superintendent of Documents, Attn: Chief, Mail List Branch, Mail Stop: SSOM, Washington, DC 20402-9375.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [18, 732, 173, 761], \"page_id\": 175}], \"content\": \"New Subscribers\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [20, 761, 628, 794], \"page_id\": 175}], \"content\": \"To order a new subscription ... please use the order form provided below.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [202, 855, 785, 892], \"page_id\": 175}], \"content\": \"Superintendent of Documents Subscriptions Order Form\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [16, 882, 1079, 1427], \"page_id\": 175}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Order Processing Code<br>*6160</td><td colspan=\\\"3\\\">Charge your order.<br>It's Easy!</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"2\\\">YES, enter my subscription(s) as follows:</td><td colspan=\\\"2\\\">To fax your orders (202) 512-2233</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"2\\\"><input type=\\\"checkbox\\\"> subscriptions of TREASURY BULLETIN, TRBU, for $29.00 per year.</td><td colspan=\\\"2\\\"><img src=\\\"MasterCard.png\\\" alt=\\\"MasterCard\\\"> <img src=\\\"VISA.png\\\" alt=\\\"VISA\\\"></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"2\\\"><input type=\\\"checkbox\\\"> subscriptions of DAILY TREASURY STATEMENT, DTS, for $174.00 per year.</td><td colspan=\\\"2\\\"></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"2\\\"><input type=\\\"checkbox\\\"> subscriptions of MONTHLY TREASURY STATEMENT, MT, for $22.00 per year.</td><td colspan=\\\"2\\\"></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"4\\\">The total cost of my order is $__________. International customers please add 25%. Prices include regular domestic postage and handling and are subject to change.</td></tr><tr><td>(Company or Personal Name)</td><td colspan=\\\"3\\\">Please Choose Method of Payment:</td></tr><tr><td>(Please type or print)</td><td><in