ows the Secretary of the Treasury to borrow money by issuing Treasury securities. The Secretary determines the terms and conditions of issue, conversion, maturity, payment, and interest rate. New issues of Treasury notes mature in 2 to 10 years. Bonds mature in more than 10 years from the issue date. Each marketable security is listed in the Monthly Statement of the Public Debt of the United States. The information in this section of the \\\"Treasury Bulletin\\\" pertains only to marketable Treasury securities, current bills, notes, and bonds.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [22, 548, 673, 716], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"Table PDO-1 provides a maturity schedule of interest-bearing marketable public debt securities other than regular weekly and 52-week bills. All unmatured Treasury notes and bonds are listed in maturity order, from earliest to latest. A separate breakout is provided for the combined holdings of the Government accounts and Federal Reserve banks, so that the \\\"all other investors\\\" category includes all private holdings.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [22, 738, 673, 855], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"Table PDO-2 presents the results of weekly auctions of 13- and 26-week bills, as well as auctions of 52-week bills, which are held every fourth week. Treasury bills mature each Thursday. New issues of 13-week bills are reopenings of 26-week bills. The 26-week bill issued every fourth week to mature on the same Thursday as an existing\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [718, 318, 1372, 435], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"52-week bill is a reopening of the existing 52-week bill. New issues of cash management bills are also presented. High, low, and average yields on accepted tenders and the dollar value of total bids are presented, with the dollar value of awards made on both competitive and noncompetitive basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [720, 448, 1372, 519], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"Treasury accepts noncompetitive tenders of up to $1 million for bills and $5 million for notes and bonds in each auction of securities to encourage participation of individuals and smaller institutions.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [720, 541, 1372, 682], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"Table PDO-3 lists the results of auctions of marketable securities, other than weekly bills, in chronological order over the past 2 years. Included are: notes and bonds from table PDO-1; 52-week bills from table PDO-2; and data for cash management bills. The maturities of cash management bills coincide with those of regular issues of Treasury bills.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [720, 700, 1372, 795], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"Table PDO-4 indicates the total amount of marketable securities allotted to each class of investor. The Federal Reserve banks tally into investor classes the tenders in each auction of marketable securities other than weekly auctions of 13- and 26-week bills.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [574, 67, 940, 92], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"PUBLIC DEBT OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1395, 65, 1431, 92], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"39\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [320, 264, 1192, 297], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: OCTOBER-DECEMBER\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [70, 338, 736, 499], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [73, 521, 360, 552], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"Auction of 7-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [73, 583, 736, 818], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"September 30 Treasury announced it would auction $9,750 million of 7-year notes to refund $6,190 million of notes maturing October 15, 1992, and to raise about $3,550 million of new cash. The notes offered were Treasury notes of Series H-1999, dated October 15, 1992, due October 15, 1999, with interest payable on April 15 and October 15 until maturity. An interest rate of 6 percent was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [75, 827, 733, 1120], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"Tenders for the notes were received prior to 12 noon, e.d.s.t., for noncompetitive tenders and prior to 1 p.m., e.d.s.t., for competitive tenders on October 7, 1992, and totaled $19,584 million, of which $9,754 million was accepted at yields ranging from 5.99 percent, price 100.056, up to 6.05 percent, price 99.718. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 20 percent. Noncompetitive tenders were accepted in full at the average yield, 6.01 percent, price 99.944. These totaled $324 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $9,430 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [73, 1131, 735, 1274], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $9,754 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $473 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities, and $97 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks for their own account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [71, 1310, 491, 1339], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"Auction of 2-Year and 5-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [75, 1370, 740, 1518], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"October 21 Treasury announced it would auction $15,000 million of 2-year notes of Series AF-1994 and $10,750 million of 5-year notes of Series S-1997 to refund $12,730 million of securities maturing October 31 and to raise about $13,025 million of new cash.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [73, 1527, 736, 1672], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"The notes of Series AF-1994 were dated November 2, 1992, due October 31, 1994, with interest payable on April 30 and October 31 until maturity. An interest rate of 4-1/4 percent was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [73, 1683, 733, 1887], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"Tenders for the notes were received prior to 12 noon, e.s.t., for noncompetitive tenders and prior to 1 p.m., e.s.t, for competitive tenders on October 27, and totaled $49,870 million, of which $15,087 million was accepted. All competitive tenders at yields lower than 4.37 percent were accepted in full. Tenders at 4.37 percent were allotted 12 percent. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [778, 349, 1435, 579], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"the high yield of 4.37 percent with an equivalent price of 99.773. The median yield was 4.35 percent; that is, 50 percent of the amount of accepted competitive bids were tendered at or below that yield. The low yield was 4.30 percent; that is, 5 percent of the amount of accepted competitive bids were tendered at or below that yield. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $870 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $14,217 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [778, 590, 1433, 735], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $15,087 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $523 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities, and $634 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks for their own account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [778, 747, 1431, 887], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"The notes of Series S-1997 were dated November 2, 1992, due October 31, 1997, with interest payable on April 30 and October 31 until maturity. An interest rate of 5-3/4 percent was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [778, 901, 1433, 1339], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"Tenders for the notes were received prior to 12 noon, e.s.t., for noncompetitive tenders and prior to 1 p.m., e.s.t., for competitive tenders on October 28, and totaled $27,200 million, of which $10,753 million was accepted. All competitive tenders at yields lower than 5.84 percent were accepted in full. Tenders at 5.84 percent were allotted 87 percent. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 5.84 percent with an equivalent price of 99.615. The median yield was 5.79 percent; that is, 50 percent of the amount of accepted competitive bids were tendered at or below that yield. The low yield was 5.73 percent; that is, 5 percent of the amount of accepted competitive bids were tendered at or below that yield. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $508 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $10,245 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [775, 1350, 1431, 1496], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $10,753 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $348 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities, and $250 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks for their own account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [775, 1531, 939, 1563], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"52-Week Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [773, 1594, 1430, 1855], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"October 9 tenders were invited for approximately $14,250 million of 364-day Treasury bills to be dated October 22, 1992, and to mature October 21, 1993. The issue was to refund $13,075 million of maturing 52-week bills and to raise about $1,175 million of new cash. The bills were auctioned on October 15. They totaled $36,191 million, of which $14,274 million was accepted, including $356 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public and $3,765 million of the bills issued to Federal Reserve banks for themselves and as agents for\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [38, 33, 65, 55], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"40\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [532, 35, 891, 60], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"PUBLIC DEBT OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [237, 232, 1184, 267], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: OCTOBER-DECEMBER, con.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [38, 318, 687, 369], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"foreign and international monetary authorities. The average bank discount rate was 3.12 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [285, 462, 441, 486], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"NOVEMBER\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [38, 581, 398, 607], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"November Quarterly Financing\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [35, 645, 685, 815], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"November 3 Treasury announced it would auction $15,500 million of 3-year notes of Series R-1995, $11,250 million of 9-3/4-year 6-3/8 percent notes of Series B-2002, and $10,250 million of 30-year bonds of November 2022 to refund $23,096 million of Treasury securities maturing November 15 and to raise about $13,900 million of new cash.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [35, 828, 685, 970], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"The notes of Series R-1995 were dated November 16, 1992, due November 15, 1995, with interest payable on May 15 and November 15 until maturity. An interest rate of 5-1/8 percent was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [35, 985, 685, 1270], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"Tenders for the notes were received prior to 12 noon, e.s.t., for noncompetitive tenders and prior to 1 p.m., e.s.t., for competitive tenders on November 9, and totaled $36,118 million, of which $15,557 million was accepted at yields ranging from 5.16 percent, price 99.904, up to 5.18 percent, price 99.849. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 90 percent. Noncompetitive tenders were accepted in full at the average yield, 5.17 percent, price 99.877. These totaled $530 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $15,027 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [35, 1285, 685, 1427], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $15,557 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $701 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities, and $2,895 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks for their own account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [35, 1440, 685, 1637], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"The 6-3/8 percent notes of Series B-2002 were an additional issue of notes dated August 15, 1992, issued November 16, 1992, due August 15, 2002, with interest payable on February 15 and August 15 until maturity. Accrued interest of $16.11073 per $1,000, covering the period from August 15, 1992, to November 16, 1992, was payable with each accepted tender.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [35, 1652, 685, 1851], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"Tenders for the notes were received prior to 12 noon, e.s.t., for noncompetitive tenders and prior to 1 p.m., e.s.t., for competitive tenders on November 10, and totaled $31,057 million, of which $11,300 million was accepted at yields ranging from 6.92 percent, price 96.155, up to 6.94 percent, price 96.018. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 14 percent. Noncompetitive tenders were accepted in full at the\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [735, 318, 1383, 400], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"average yield, 6.93 percent, price 96.086. These totaled $393 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $10,907 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [735, 413, 1383, 497], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $11,300 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $800 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks for their own account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [736, 510, 1383, 563], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"The notes of Series B-2002 may be held in STRIPS form. The minimum par amount required is $1,600,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [735, 576, 1383, 806], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"The bonds of November 2022 were dated November 15, 1992, issued November 16, 1992, due November 15, 2022, with interest payable on May 15 and November 15 until maturity. An interest rate of 7-5/8 percent was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis. Accrued interest of $0.21064 per $1,000, covering the period from November 15, 1992, to November 16, 1992, was payable with each accepted tender.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [733, 822, 1383, 1109], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"Tenders for the bonds were received prior to 12 noon, e.s.t., for noncompetitive tenders and prior to 1 p.m., e.s.t., for competitive tenders on November 12, and totaled $25,615 million, of which $10,298 million was accepted at yields ranging from 7.65 percent, price 99.707, up to 7.66 percent, price 99.590. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 66 percent. Noncompetitive tenders were accepted in full at the average yield, 7.66 percent, price 99.590. These totaled $322 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $9,976 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [733, 1122, 1383, 1204], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $10,298 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $400 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks for their own account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [733, 1219, 1382, 1270], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"The bonds of November 2022 may be held in STRIPS form. The minimum par amount required is $1,600,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [733, 1312, 1136, 1336], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"Auction of 2-Year and 5-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [733, 1374, 1382, 1513], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"November 18 Treasury announced it would auction $15,000 million of 2-year notes of Series AG-1994 and $10,750 million of 5-year notes of Series T-1997 to refund $13,332 million of securities maturing November 30 and to raise about $12,425 million of new cash.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [733, 1528, 1382, 1670], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"The notes of Series AG-1994 were dated November 30, 1992, due November 30, 1994, with interest payable on May 31 and November 30 until maturity. An interest rate of 4-5/8 percent was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [731, 1683, 1382, 1851], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"Tenders for the notes were received prior to 12 noon, e.s.t., for noncompetitive tenders and prior to 1 p.m., e.s.t., for competitive tenders on November 23, and totaled $44,622 million, of which $15,010 million was accepted. All competitive tenders at yields lower than 4.72 percent were accepted in full. Tenders at 4.72 percent were allotted 35 percent. All noncom-\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 22, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [559, 58, 929, 94], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"PUBLIC DEBT OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1385, 54, 1430, 87], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"41\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [267, 255, 1227, 295], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: OCTOBER-DECEMBER, con.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [65, 335, 733, 606], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"petitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 4.72 percent with an equivalent price of 99.821. The median yield was 4.70 percent; that is, 50 percent of the amount of accepted competitive bids were tendered at or below that yield. The low yield was 4.68 percent; that is, 5 percent of the amount of accepted competitive bids were tendered at or below that yield. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $652 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $14,358 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [58, 608, 728, 756], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $15,010 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $498 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities, and $370 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks for their own account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [58, 758, 726, 914], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"The notes of Series T-1997 were dated November 30, 1992, due November 30, 1997, with interest payable on May 31 and November 30 until maturity. An interest rate of 6 percent was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [65, 917, 733, 1366], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"Tenders for the notes were received prior to 12 noon, e.s.t., for noncompetitive tenders and prior to 1 p.m., e.s.t., for competitive tenders on November 24, and totaled $27,133 million, of which $10,753 million was accepted. All competitive tenders at yields lower than 6.07 percent were accepted in full. Tenders at 6.07 percent were allotted 34 percent. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 6.07 percent with an equivalent price of 99.702. The median yield was 6.02 percent; that is, 50 percent of the amount of accepted competitive bids were tendered at or below that yield. The low yield was 5.95 percent; that is, 5 percent of the amount of accepted competitive bids were tendered at or below that yield. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $601 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $10,152 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [63, 1366, 731, 1518], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $10,753 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $598 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities, and $150 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks for their own account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [66, 1549, 245, 1587], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"52-Week Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [66, 1610, 731, 1885], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"November 6 tenders were invited for approximately $14,250 million of 364-day Treasury bills to be dated November 19, 1992, and to mature November 18, 1993. The issue was to refund $12,276 million of maturing 52-week bills and to raise about $1,975 million of new cash. The bills were auctioned on November 17. They totaled $34,410 million, of which $14,255 million was accepted, including $367 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public and $3,590 million of the bills issued to Federal Reserve banks for themselves and as agents for\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [763, 333, 1425, 402], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"foreign and international monetary authorities. The average bank discount rate was 3.61 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [766, 429, 1047, 463], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [765, 490, 1433, 695], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"October 30 tenders were invited for approximately $15,000 million of 41-day bills to be issued November 6, 1992, representing an additional amount of bills dated December 19, 1991, maturing December 17, 1992. The issue was to raise new cash. Tenders were opened on November 5. They totaled $43,767 million, of which $15,042 million was accepted. The average bank discount rate was 3 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [763, 709, 1431, 867], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [758, 890, 1184, 932], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"Auction of 2-Year and 5-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [765, 957, 1436, 1111], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"December 16 Treasury announced it would auction $15,500 million of 2-year notes of Series AH-1994 and $11,250 million of 5-year notes of Series U-1997 to refund $20,954 million of securities maturing December 31 and to raise about $5,800 million of new cash.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [761, 1111, 1436, 1268], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"The notes of Series AH-1994 were dated December 31, 1992, due December 31, 1994, with interest payable on June 30 and December 31 until maturity. An interest rate of 4-5/8 percent was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [763, 1270, 1430, 1453], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"Tenders for the notes were received prior to 12 noon, e.s.t., for noncompetitive tenders and prior to 1 p.m., e.s.t., for competitive tenders on December 22, and totaled $39,039 million, of which $15,501 million was accepted. All competitive tenders at yields lower than 4.71 percent were accepted in full. Tenders at 4.71 percent were allotted 27 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [766, 1453, 1435, 1551], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 4.71 percent with an equivalent price of 99.840.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [760, 1551, 1435, 1762], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"The median yield was 4.68 percent; that is, 50 percent of the amount of accepted competitive bids were tendered at or below that yield. The low yield was 4.65 percent; that is, 5 percent of the amount of accepted competitive bids were tendered at or below that yield. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $1,045 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $14,456 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [766, 1762, 1430, 1862], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $15,501 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $503 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international mone-\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [36, 44, 61, 68], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"42\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [529, 42, 887, 68], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"PUBLIC DEBT OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [234, 243, 1182, 274], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: OCTOBER-DECEMBER, con.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [35, 331, 683, 382], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"tary authorities, and $1,100 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks for their own account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [35, 395, 683, 541], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"The notes of Series U-1997 were dated December 31, 1992, due December 31, 1997, with interest payable on June 30 and December 31 until maturity. An interest rate of 6 percent was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [35, 557, 685, 987], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"Tenders for the notes were received prior to 12 noon, e.s.t., for noncompetitive tenders and prior to 1 p.m., e.s.t., for competitive tenders on December 23, and totaled $24,459 million, of which $11,260 million was accepted. All competitive tenders at yields lower than 6.03 percent were accepted in full. Tenders at 6.03 percent were allotted 62 percent. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 6.03 percent with an equivalent price of 99.872. The median yield was 5.97 percent; that is, 50 percent of the amount of accepted competitive bids were tendered at or below that yield. The low yield was 5.90 percent; that is, 5 percent of the amount of accepted competitive bids were tendered at or below that yield. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $870 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $10,390 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [35, 1001, 685, 1084], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $11,260 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $398 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international mone-\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [730, 298, 1382, 351], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"tary authorities, and $470 million was accepted from Federal Reserve banks for their own account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [730, 391, 879, 417], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"52-Week Bill\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [730, 453, 1383, 773], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"December 4 tenders were invited for approximately $14,750 million of 364-day Treasury bills to be dated December 17, 1992, and to mature December 16, 1993. The issue was to refund $13,354 million of maturing 52-week bills and to raise about $1,400 million of new cash. The bills were auctioned on December 10. They totaled $35,136 million, of which $14,775 million was accepted, including $326 million of non-competitive tenders from the public and $3,840 million of the bills issued to Federal Reserve banks for themselves and as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities. The average bank discount rate was 3.57 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [733, 811, 1002, 837], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [731, 872, 1383, 1076], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"November 27 tenders were invited for approximately $16,000 million of 49-day bills to be issued December 3, 1992, representing an additional amount of bills dated July 23, 1992, maturing January 21, 1993. The issue was to raise new cash. Tenders were opened on December 1. They totaled $35,738 million, of which $16,008 million was accepted. The average bank discount rate was 3.29 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [564, 56, 944, 96], \"page_id\": 53}], \"content\": \"PUBLIC DEBT OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1383, 60, 1436, 103], \"page_id