\"page_id\": 149}], \"content\": \"The LUST trust fund is financed by taxes collected on gasoline, diesel fuels, special motor fuels, aviation fuels, and fuels used in commercial transportation on inland waterways. Amounts available in the Lust trust fund, exceeding current expenditure requirements, are\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [773, 324, 1421, 396], \"page_id\": 149}], \"content\": \"invested by the Secretary of the Treasury in interest-bearing Government securities (e.g., Treasury bills). All interest earned is credited directly to the LUST trust fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [775, 405, 1423, 476], \"page_id\": 149}], \"content\": \"To carry out the LUST program, amounts are appropriated for the LUST trust fund to the Environmental Protection Agency for programmatic and administrative expenses.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [771, 485, 1425, 601], \"page_id\": 149}], \"content\": \"An annual report to Congress by the Secretary of the Treasury is required by 26 U.S.C. 9602 (a). These reports present the financial condition of the LUST trust fund and results of operations for the past fiscal year, and its expected condition and operations during the next fiscal 5 years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [348, 715, 1156, 787], \"page_id\": 149}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-17.--Leaking Underground Storage Tank Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal 1992\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [609, 805, 901, 834], \"page_id\": 149}], \"content\": \"(Source. Financial Management Service)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [70, 852, 1426, 1359], \"page_id\": 149}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 1991</td><td>$470,149,000</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><t