 strategy to improve the quality of creditors' assets and creditworthiness in debtor countries.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [161, 921, 1144, 950], \"page_id\": 22}], \"content\": \"\\\"U.S. Policy Toward Direct Foreign Investment.\\\" Robson, John E. March 1990, pp. 4-7.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [184, 950, 1295, 979], \"page_id\": 22}], \"content\": \"An exploration into the position that the United States is taking on foreign trade and investment policy matters.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [161, 1070, 386, 1113], \"page_id\": 22}], \"content\": \"Tax Policy\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [161, 1193, 1276, 1222], \"page_id\": 22}], \"content\": \"Congressional Reports and Staff Working Papers by the Office of Tax Policy. March 1988, pp. 3-4.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [184, 1222, 1322, 1278], \"page_id\": 22}], \"content\": \"A listing of research studies pertaining to important contemporary and anticipated tax policy issues, particularly related to the 1986-7 tax reform effort.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [161, 1329, 1320, 1385], \"page_id\": 22}], \"content\": \"\\\"Effect of the Tax Reform Act of 1986 on Commercial Banks, The.\\\" Excerpted. Neubig, Thomas S., and Martin A. Sullivan. June 1988, pp. 3-7.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [192, 1385, 1320, 1438], \"page_id\": 22}], \"content\": \"An analysis of the overall effect of tax reform on the banking industry, which, the study concludes, benefits from tax reform.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [164, 1492, 1322, 1548], \"page_id\": 22}], \"content\": \"\\\"Impact of the Tax Reform Act of 1986 on Trade and Capital Flows, The.\\\" Excerpted. Grubert, Harry, and John Mutti. March 1988, pp. 5-8.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [187, 1548, 1322, 1603], \"page_id\": 22}], \"content\": \"An analysis of the international implications of tax reform, based on a general equilibrium model of the United States and the rest of the world.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [162, 1657, 1322, 1737], \"page_id\": 22}], \"content\": \"\\\"New Estimates of Capital Gains Realization Behavior: Evidence from Pooled Cross-Section Data.\\\" Summary. Gillingham, Robert, John S. Greenlees, and Kimberly D. Zieschang. September 1989, pp. 4-5.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [184, 1737, 1322, 1820], \"page_id\": 22}], \"content\": \"A paper developing and estimating a behavioral model of taxpayer response to capital gains taxation. Using the econometric approach, the pooled cross-section data represents a set of independent observations from a taxpayer sampling extending over the period 1977-85.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1411, 46, 1431, 66], \"page_id\": 23}], \"content\": \"9\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [585, 91, 937, 130], \"page_id\": 23}], \"content\": \"TREASURY ISSUES INDEX\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [182, 201, 1343, 261], \"page_id\": 23}], \"content\": \"\\\"Noncorporate Business Taxation: Before and After the Tax Reform Act of 1986.\\\" Excerpted. Nelson, Susan C. December 1988, pp. 8-12.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [216, 261, 1347, 342], \"page_id\": 23}], \"content\": \"An analysis of the effects that the Tax Reform Act of 1986 might have on noncorporate business in terms of