 (Freedom Shares) on sale from May 1, 1967, through June 30, 1970, to E bond buyers.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [65, 54, 102, 85], \"page_id\": 72}], \"content\": \"58\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [64, 274, 724, 399], \"page_id\": 72}], \"content\": \"Federal securities presented in these tables comprise public debt securities issued by the Treasury and debt issued by other Federal agencies under special financing authorities. See the Federal debt (FD) series of tables for a more complete description of the Federal debt.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [62, 419, 723, 475], \"page_id\": 72}], \"content\": \"Table OFS-1.--Distribution of Federal Securities by Class of Investors and Type of Issues\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [60, 493, 724, 665], \"page_id\": 72}], \"content\": \"Holdings of Treasury marketable and nonmarketable securities and of debt issued by other Federal agencies are presented for Government accounts, the Federal Reserve banks, and private investors. Government account holdings largely reflect investment by the social security and Federal retirement trust funds. The Federal Reserve banks acquire Treasury securities in the market as a means of executing monetary policy.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [480, 125, 1002, 154], \"page_id\": 72}], \"content\": \"OWNERSHIP OF FEDERAL SECURITIES\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [636, 190, 850, 225], \"page_id\": 72}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [760, 274, 1419, 330], \"page_id\": 72}], \"content\": \"Table OFS-2.--Estimated Ownership of Public Debt Securities Held by Private Investors\", \"descript