d>4,964</td><td>5,585</td><td>6,062</td><td>6,550</td><td>7,159</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>1,331</td><td>1,337</td><td>1,352</td><td>1,374</td><td>1,394</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>6,295</td><td>6,922</td><td>7,414</td><td>7,924</td><td>8,553</td></tr><tr><td>Outlays 1</td><td>5,371</td><td>5,765</td><td>6,307</td><td>6,757</td><td>7,023</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30 2</td><td>15,279</td><td>16,436</td><td>17,543</td><td>18,710</td><td>20,240</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [67, 506, 724, 560], \"page_id\": 132}], \"content\": \"Outlays include $35 million for 1991 and 1992, and $36 million 1993 through 1995, for the Department of Commerce, National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration. Outlays also include $29 million for rental payments to General Services Administration in 1991. Essen-\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [766, 504, 1415, 560], \"page_id\": 132}], \"content\": \"tial Air Service outlays include $23 million for 1992, and $39 million for 1993 through 1995. 2 Large portions of the unexpended balance are committed to liquidate outstanding unfunded obligations (contract authority) and to liquidate unexpended appropriations.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1386, 51, 1436, 84], \"page_id\": 133}], \"content\": \"119\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [589, 124, 909, 166], \"page_id\": 133}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUND REPORTS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [338, 305, 1242, 499], \"page_id\": 133}], \"content\": \"RECEIPTS AND OUTLAYS AIRPORT AND AIRWAY TRUST FUND Fiscal Years 1986-90\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [51, 506, 1436, 1718], \"page_id\": 133}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [660, 1740, 907, 1782], \"page_id\": 133}], \"content\": \"FISCAL YEARS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [54, 51, 119, 87], \"page_id\": 134}], \"content\": \"120\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [591, 83, 875, 118], \"page_id\": 134}], \"content\": \"Asbestos Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [45, 174, 718, 361], \"page_id\": 134}], \"content\": \"The asbestos trust fund was established on the books of the Treasury in fiscal 1987 pursuant to Public Law 99-519, Oct. 22, 1986. It consists of amounts received in the Treasury on or after Jan. 1, 1987, as repayments of loans made under section 505 of the Asbestos School Hazard Abatement Act of 1984 (20 U.S.C. 4011 et seq.), and amounts received as deposits from local educational agencies under section 207(a) of the Toxic Substances Control Act.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [52, 359, 713, 439], \"page_id\": 134}], \"content\": \"Amounts available in the fund in excess of current outlay requirements are invested in interest-bearing obligations of the United States, and any interest earned and proceeds from sale or redemp-\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [751, 169, 1029, 201], \"page_id\": 134}], \"content\": \"tion are credited to the fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [753, 203, 1419, 308], \"page_id\": 134}], \"content\": \"Amounts are made available to the Environmental Protection Agency for the purpose of carrying out the school loan and grant program under section 505 of the Asbestos School Hazard Abatement Act.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [755, 305, 1425, 410], \"page_id\": 134}], \"content\": \"Annual reports to the Congress are required of the Secretary of the Treasury each year on the financial condition and results of the operations of the trust fund for the preceding fiscal year and on its expected condition and operations during the next 5 fiscal years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [529, 471, 944, 502], \"page_id\": 134}], \"content\": \"Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 1990\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [579, 502, 893, 531], \"page_id\": 134}], \"content\": \"[Source: Financial Management Service]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [50, 537, 1419, 734], \"page_id\": 134}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 1989</td><td>$7,811,843</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Loan repayments</td><td>6,184,000</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>770,804</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments\\u2014accrued</td><td>100,166</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>7,054,971</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30, 1990</td><td>14,866,814</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [380, 772, 1092, 805], \"page_id\": 134}], \"content\": \"Expected Condition and Results of Operations, Fiscal Years 1991-95\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [688, 809, 786, 836], \"page_id\": 134}], \"content\": \"{In millions}\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [54, 836, 1417, 1142], \"page_id\": 134}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th></th><th>1991</th><th>1992</th><th>1993</th><th>1994</th><th>1995</th></tr><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1</td><td>$14.8</td><td>$21.9</td><td>$33.2</td><td>$46.4</td><td>$60.5</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Loan repayments</td><td>6.2</td><td>9.9</td><td>11.6</td><td>12.5</td><td>13.5</td></tr><tr><td>Fines and penalties</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>.9</td><td>1.4</td><td>1.6</td><td>1.6</td><td>1.7</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>7.1</td><td>11.3</td><td>13.2</td><td>14.1</td><td>15.2</td></tr><tr><td>Outlays</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30</td><td>21.9</td><td>33.2</td><td>46.4</td><td>60.5</td><td>75.7</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [542, 77, 964, 108], \"page_id\": 135}], \"content\": \"Black Lung Disability Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1377, 40, 1431, 80], \"page_id\": 135}], \"content\": \"121\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [75, 146, 733, 508], \"page_id\": 135}], \"content\": \"The black lung disability trust fund was established on the books of the Treasury in fiscal 1978 pursuant to the Black Lung Benefits Revenue Act of 1977. Public Law 97-119, Dec. 29, 1981, entitled \\\"Trust Fund Code of 1981\\\" (26 U.S.C. 9501), provides for the continuation of the fund as previously established under section 3 of the act of 1977. The Consolidated Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1985 (Public Law 99-272), enacted Apr. 7, 1986, provided for an increase in the coal tax effective Apr. 1, 1986, through Dec. 31, 1995, and a 5-year forgiveness of interest retroactive to Oct. 1, 1985. The 5-year moratorium on interest payments ended on Sept. 30, 1990. Payment of interest on advances resumes in fiscal 1991. The Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1987 (Public Law 100-203), signed Dec. 22, 1987, extends the temporary increase in the coal tax through Dec. 31, 2013.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [75, 506, 731, 685], \"page_id\": 135}], \"content\": \"The act designates the following receipts to be appropriated and transferred from the general fund of the Treasury to the trust fund: excise taxes on mined coal tonnage; taxable expenditures of private black lung benefit trusts; reimbursements by responsible mine operators; and related fines, penalties, and interest charges. Estimates made by the Secretary of the Treasury determine monthly transfers of amounts for excise taxes to the trust fund, subject to\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [766, 146, 1260, 170], \"page_id\": 135}], \"content\": \"adjustments in later transfers to actual tax receipts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [770, 174, 1431, 322], \"page_id\": 135}], \"content\": \"Amounts available in the fund in excess of current expenditure requirements are invested by the Secretary of the Treasury in interest-bearing public debt securities, and any interest earned is credited to the fund. Also credited to the fund, if necessary, are repayable advances from the general fund to meet outlay require-ments in excess of available revenues.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [773, 325, 1433, 479], \"page_id\": 135}], \"content\": \"To carry out the black lung disability program, amounts are made available to the Department of Labor. Other charges to the fund are to pay administrative expenses incurred by the Department of Health and Human Services and the Department of the Treasury, and also to repay advances from the general fund and interest on advances.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [775, 477, 1431, 643], \"page_id\": 135}], \"content\": \"The act requires the Secretary of the Treasury to submit an annual report to Congress after consultation with the Secretary of Labor and the Secretary of Health and Human Services (26 U.S.C. 9602 (a)). The report must present the financial condition and results of operations of the fund during the past fiscal year and the expected condition and operations of the fund during the next 5 fiscal years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [551, 731, 967, 764], \"page_id\": 135}], \"content\": \"Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 1990\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [600, 771, 901, 795], \"page_id\": 135}], \"content\": \"[Source: Financial Management Service]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [65, 802, 1431, 1299], \"page_id\": 135}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 1989</td><td>$4,009,578</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Excise taxes (transferred from general fund):</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>$1.10 tax on underground coal</td><td>300,932,000</td></tr><tr><td>$0.55 tax on surface coal</td><td>167,949,000</td></tr><tr><td>4.4-percent tax on underground coal</td><td>123,434,000</td></tr><tr><td>4.4-percent tax on surface coal</td><td>73,033,000</td></tr><tr><td>Fines, penalties, and interest</td><td>7,190,467</td></tr><tr><td>Collection-responsible mine operators</td><td>14,007,422</td></tr><tr><td>Repayable advances from the general fund</td><td>154,611</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>686,700,500</td></tr><tr><td>Net receipts</td><td>686,700,500</td></tr><tr><td>Outlays:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Treasury administrative expenses</td><td>540,618</td></tr><tr><td>Salaries and expenses-Labor-DM</td><td>22,535,700</td></tr><tr><td>Salaries and expenses-Labor-ESA</td><td>28,640,000</td></tr><tr><td>Total outlays</td><td>51,716,318</td></tr><tr><td>Expenses:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Program expense-Labor</td><td>573,359,637</td></tr><tr><td>Total expenses</td><td>573,359,637</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30, 1990</td><td>65,634,123</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [400, 1323, 1101, 1354], \"page_id\": 135}], \"content\": \"Expected Condition and Results of Operations, Fiscal Years 1991-95\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [697, 1365, 806, 1389], \"page_id\": 135}], \"content\": \"(In thousands)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [66, 1391, 1436, 1752], \"page_id\": 135}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th></th><th>1991</th><th>1992</th><th>1993</th><th>1994</th><th>1995</th></tr><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1.</td><td>$65,634</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Excise taxes</td><td>627,000</td><td>$649,000</td><td>$667,000</td><td>$680,000</td><td>$694,000</td></tr><tr><td>Advances from general fund</td><td>278,990</td><td>319,000</td><td>323,000</td><td>335,000</td><td>344,000</td></tr><tr><td>Fines, penalties, and interest</td><td>2,000</td><td>2,000</td><td>2,000</td><td>2,000</td><td>2,000</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>907,990</td><td>970,000</td><td>992,000</td><td>1,017,000</td><td>1,040,000</td></tr><tr><td>Outlays:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Benefit payments</td><td>592,426</td><td>570,187</td><td>569,187</td><td>571,187</td><td>572,187</td></tr><tr><td>Administrative expenses</td><td>53,198</td><td>56,813</td><td>56,813</td><td>56,813</td><td>56,813</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on repayable advances</td><td>328,000</td><td>343,000</td><td>366,000</td><td>389,000</td><td>411,000</td></tr><tr><td>Total outlays</td><td>973,624</td><td>970,000</td><td>992,000</td><td>1,017,000</td><td>1,040,000</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [65, 47, 109, 71], \"page_id\": 136}], \"content\": \"122\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [540, 78, 942, 103], \"page_id\": 136}], \"content\": \"Harbor Maintenance Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [62, 147, 716, 250], \"page_id\": 136}], \"content\": \"The harbor maintenance trust fund was established on the books of the Treasury on Apr. 1, 1987, in accordance with the Water Resources Development Act of 1986 (Public Law 99-962, Nov. 17, 1986) (26 U.S.C. 9505).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [62, 250, 716, 428], \"page_id\": 136}], \"content\": \"The harbor maintenance trust fund consists of such amounts as may be appropriated as provided in section 9505(b), transferred by the Saint Lawrence Seaway Development Corporation (SLSDC) pursuant to section 13(a) of the Act of May 13, 1954, or credited as provided in section 9602(b). Amounts are appropriated equivalent to the taxes received in the Treasury under section 4461 (relating to harbor maintenance tax).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [62, 433, 718, 665], \"page_id\": 136}], \"content\": \"Amounts in the harbor maintenance trust fund shall be available as provided by appropriation acts for making expenditures to carry out section 210(a) of the Water Resources Development Act of 1986, for payments of rebates of tolls or charges pursuant to section 13(b) of the Act of May 13, 1954 (as in effect on Apr. 1, 1987), and for the payment of all expenses of administration incurred by the Department of the Treasury in administering subchapter A of chapter 36 (relating to harbor maintenance tax), but not in excess of $5,000,000 for any fiscal year and for periods during which no fee applies under\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [765, 147, 1415, 323], \"page_id\": 136}], \"content\": \"paragraph (9) or (10) of section 13031(a) of the Consolidated Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1985. The provision in the act for payment of the expenses of the administration costs from this source has been found to be in violation with the General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade (GATT). Therefore, legislation is proposed to authorize payment of all expenses for administration costs from the harbor maintenance trust fund itself.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [763, 332, 1414, 504], \"page_id\": 136}], \"content\": \"The harbor maintenance user fee was increased by the Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1990 (Public Law 101-508, approved Nov. 5, 1990). The ad valorem user fee imposed on applicable commercial cargo increased from 0.04 percent to 0.125 percent. The Water Resources Development Act of 1990 increased to 100 percent the amount of the harbor maintenance costs that can be financed by the trust fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [763, 508, 1414, 640], \"page_id\": 136}], \"content\": \"Annual reports to Congress are required by 26 U.S.C. 9505 to be submitted by the Secretary of the Treasury. These reports are required to cover the financial condition and the results of operations of the fund during the past fiscal year and its expected condition and operations during the next 5 fiscal years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [537, 716, 944, 740], \"page_id\": 136}], \"content\": \"Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 1990\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [594, 747, 885, 774], \"page_id\": 136}], \"content\": \"(Source: Financial Management Service)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [59, 776, 1385, 1142], \"page_id\": 136}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 1989</td><td>$12,311,488</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Excis